{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0127bGTzNnsFdTjnY2WH8zVj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Layer hierarchy 无法作为 headline claim。5-model pooled layer gap\n2\t  仅 ~4pp (p=0.14, n.s.)， 被 model×type interaction (p=0.008) 瓦解——type ranking 因模型架构而异\n3\t  (GPT 系 spec>ling, Qwen3-8B 反转, Claude 混合)。Judge calibration 暴露 coreferential (F1=0.61)\n4\t  和 auth_scope (F1=0.68) 的 type-specific measurement bias， 进一步削弱 type-level claims。Error\n5\t  analysis failure mode 跨层重叠 42%，无 clean mechanism 区分。 首选 reframe: (C) \"The Massive\n6\t  Binary Effect\" 为 primary——+30pp 仍是文献最大因果效应 + perturbation control PASS (Δ=4.2pp,\n7\t  ratio=0.13)；(B) \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 为 §6 核心—— 92% traces 中 agent 未识别歧义存在，universal\n8\t  across types and models。 C2 降级为 \"Model-Dependent Vulnerability Profiles\" (model×type\n9\t  interaction 从 nuisance 升级为 finding)； C3 layer claim 放弃。备选标题: \"Policy Ambiguity Causes\n10\t  Catastrophic Safety Violations in LLM Agents: A Causal Study\"。仍投 EMNLP——C1 (causal\n11\t  binary effect) + perturbation control + ambiguity blindness analysis = solid 3-contribution\n12\t  paper。\n13\t\n14\t  '\n15\timagined_experiments:\n16\t- name: full_study_clause_generation\n17\t  plan_id: plan_001\n18\t  description: '生成 140 新 clause pairs (coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20,\n19\t    incompleteness +20)， 补全 6 types × 50 pairs = 300 对。混合 CP 格式 (labeled + unlabeled)。Chantree-style\n20\t    质量验证。\n21\t\n22\t    '\n23\t  expected_results:\n24\t    total_pairs: 300\n25\t    pairs_per_type: 50\n26\t    cp_labeled_ratio: 0.5\n27\t    quality_pass_rate: 0.92\n28\t    avg_token_delta_amb_vs_unamb: 3.8\n29\t    coreferential_revision_rounds: 3\n30\t    auth_scope_revision_rounds: 2\n31\t  result_rationale: 'Clause 生成本身不受 worst tier 影响——数据准备阶段。但 quality_pass_rate 92% 而非\n32\t    >95% 因为 coreferential 的 RC attachment 与 scopal 存在边界重叠 (RC8 预示的问题)， 以及 auth_scope\n33\t    与 incompleteness 的 distinction 需要精细控制 (RC9)。 Coreferential 需要 3 轮修订 (vs 常规 1-2\n34\t    轮)：mini-pilot 会暴露 2/5 clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation，需重写。这些 clause\n35\t    层面的质量差异 会在后续实验中放大为 type-specific measurement noise。\n36\t\n37\t    '\n38\t  tables:\n39\t  - name: Clause Pair Statistics by Type\n40\t    columns:\n41\t    - type\n42\t    - n_pairs\n43\t    - avg_amb_tokens\n44\t    - avg_unamb_tokens\n45\t    - token_delta\n46\t    - quality_pass_rate\n47\t    rows:\n48\t    - - auth_scope\n49\t      - 50\n50\t      - 28.3\n51\t      - 32.1\n52\t      - 3.8\n53\t      - 0.9\n54\t    - - incompleteness\n55\t      - 50\n56\t      - 26.7\n57\t      - 30.5\n58\t      - 3.8\n59\t      - 0.94\n60\t    - - conditional_polysemy\n61\t      - 50\n62\t      - 24.2\n63\t      - 25.8\n64\t      - 1.6\n65\t      - 0.96\n66\t    - - scopal\n67\t      - 50\n68\t      - 22.5\n69\t      - 23.9\n70\t      - 1.4\n71\t      - 0.96\n72\t    - - lexical\n73\t      - 50\n74\t      - 21.8\n75\t      - 23.1\n76\t      - 1.3\n77\t      - 0.94\n78\t    - - coreferential\n79\t      - 50\n80\t      - 25.1\n81\t      - 27.4\n82\t      - 2.3\n83\t      - 0.88\n84\t  figures_description:\n85\t  - 'Token length distribution per type (box plot): spec-layer types 系统性更长，unambiguous\n86\t    版本需更多 explicit information'\n87\t  analysis: 'Coreferential quality_pass_rate 最低 (0.88)，auth_scope 0.90——这两个新 type\n88\t    的 clause 质量问题会在 plan_009 judge calibration 中以 type-specific F1 下降的形式体现。 Token\n89\t    delta spec-layer (3.8) > ling-layer (1.7) 是 potential confound， plan_004 需 report\n90\t    并控制。\n91\t\n92\t    '\n93\t- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n94\t  plan_id: plan_001b\n95\t  description: 'Coreferential + auth_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4)\n96\t    = 20 episodes。 验证新类型基本可行性。\n97\t\n98\t    '\n99\t  expected_results:\n100\t    coreferential_amb_violation_rate: 0.4\n101\t    coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n102\t    auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n103\t    auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n104\t    coreferential_binary_effect_pp: 40\n105\t    auth_scope_binary_effect_pp: 60\n106\t    systematic_issues_found: true\n107\t    issues_detail: 2/5 coreferential clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation;\n108\t      1/5 auth_scope unambiguous 版本仍残余歧义\n109\t  result_rationale: 'Mini-pilot 在 gpt-5.4 上给出 \"go\" 信号——两个新 type 均触发 violations，control\n110\t    < 15%。 但这是 worst tier 的隐患起点: gpt-5.4 的 auth_scope 60% / coreferential 40% pattern\n111\t    看似 confirm spec > ling hierarchy，但 N=5 的 CI 极宽 (±30pp)。 关键: 相同 clauses 在 Qwen3-8B\n112\t    上 profile 会反转 (coreferential ~45%, auth_scope ~28%)—— mini-pilot 仅测 1 model 无法预见跨模型\n113\t    interaction。 gpt-5.4 上 coreferential 2/5 conservative refusal 预示该 type 行为异质性高，\n114\t    但在 mini-pilot 被归为 \"fixable clause quality issue\" 而非 structural warning。\n115\t\n116\t    '\n117\t  tables:\n118\t  - name: Mini-Pilot Results\n119\t    columns:\n120\t    - type\n121\t    - condition\n122\t    - n\n123\t    - violations\n124\t    - rate\n125\t    rows:\n126\t    - - coreferential\n127\t      - ambiguous\n128\t      - 5\n129\t      - 2\n130\t      - 40%\n131\t    - - coreferential\n132\t      - unambiguous\n133\t      - 5\n134\t      - 0\n135\t      - 0%\n136\t    - - auth_scope\n137\t      - ambiguous\n138\t      - 5\n139\t      - 3\n140\t      - 60%\n141\t    - - auth_scope\n142\t      - unambiguous\n143\t      - 5\n144\t      - 0\n145\t      - 0%\n146\t  figures_description: []\n147\t  analysis: 'Mini-pilot 的 \"go\" 信号在 worst tier 下是 misleading confidence: gpt-5.4 single-model\n148\t    validation 无法检测 model-dependent vulnerability profiles。 实际需要 ≥2 model families\n149\t    的 mini-pilot 才能预见 plan_003 的 interaction 问题。\n150\t\n151\t    '\n152\t- name: perturbation_control\n153\t  plan_id: plan_010\n154\t  description: '30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs (15 synonym substitution + 15\n155\t    clause reordering) × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。验证 ambiguity-specific\n156\t    因果性。\n157\t\n158\t    '\n159\t  expected_results:\n160\t    total_episodes: 180\n161\t    perturbation_delta_pp: 4.2\n162\t    perturbation_ci: '[-1.8, 10.2]'\n163\t    ambiguity_delta_pp: 31.5\n164\t    ambiguity_ci: '[26.8, 36.2]'\n165\t    net_delta_pp: 27.3\n166\t    ratio: 0.13\n167\t    verdict: PASS\n168\t    synonym_substitution_delta_pp: 3.1\n169\t    synonym_ci: '[-3.2, 9.4]'\n170\t    clause_reordering_delta_pp: 5.3\n171\t    clause_reordering_ci: '[-0.8, 11.4]'\n172\t    ci_width_perturbation: 12.0\n173\t  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control 在 worst tier 下仍 PASS——binary effect 的因果性不受\n174\t    layer hierarchy 问题影响。 Δ_perturb=4.2pp (CI 含 0): synonym substitution (3.1pp) 和\n175\t    clause reordering (5.3pp) 均不引起 meaningful violation rate 变化。Ratio=0.13 < 0.15\n176\t    → PASS 最强形式。 Clause reordering 略高 (5.3pp) 源于轻微 primacy/recency effect，但远小于 ambiguity\n177\t    effect。 CI width 12.0pp 接近但未超过 15pp 追加阈值——worst tier 下这是 marginal 风险， 但当前数据足够。这个\n178\t    PASS 是 worst tier 的最大 silver lining: 即使 type hierarchy 崩溃，binary ambiguity effect\n179\t    仍有最强因果证据支撑， 使 reframe (C) \"Massive Binary Effect\" 有坚实因果基础。\n180\t\n181\t    '\n182\t  tables:\n183\t  - name: Perturbation Control Results\n184\t    columns:\n185\t    - condition\n186\t    - violation_rate\n187\t    - Δpp_vs_baseline\n188\t    - 95% CI\n189\t    rows:\n190\t    - - unambiguous_baseline\n191\t      - 5.5%\n192\t      - —\n193\t      - —\n194\t    - - synonym_substitution\n195\t      - 8.6%\n196\t      - +3.1pp\n197\t      - '[-3.2, 9.4]'\n198\t    - - clause_reordering\n199\t      - 10.8%\n200\t      - +5.3pp\n201\t      - '[-0.8, 11.4]'\n202\t    - - perturbation_pooled\n203\t      - 9.7%\n204\t      - +4.2pp\n205\t      - '[-1.8, 10.2]'\n206\t    - - ambiguous\n207\t      - 37.0%\n208\t      - +31.5pp\n209\t      - '[26.8, 36.2]'\n210\t  - name: Perturbation Verdict Summary\n211\t    columns:\n212\t    - metric\n213\t    - value\n214\t    - threshold\n215\t    - verdict\n216\t    rows:\n217\t    - - Δ_perturb\n218\t      - 4.2pp\n219\t      - < 5pp\n220\t      - ✓ PASS\n221\t    - - ratio\n222\t      - '0.13'\n223\t      - < 0.15\n224\t      - ✓ PASS\n225\t    - - CI_contains_0\n226\t      - 'yes'\n227\t      - required\n228\t      - ✓\n229\t    - - CI_width\n230\t      - 12.0pp\n231\t      - < 15pp\n232\t      - ✓ (marginal)\n233\t  figures_description:\n234\t  - 'Bar chart: baseline / perturbation / ambiguity 三条件 violation rate + CI — ambiguity\n235\t    远超其余两条件'\n236\t  analysis: 'PASS verdict 确保 C1 因果 claim 在任何 tier 下成立。 这是 paper 的 methodological backbone——区别于所有\n237\t    prior work (DRIP-R, PhantomPolicy 均无此控制)。\n238\t\n239\t    '\n240\t- name: full_study_api\n241\t  plan_id: plan_002\n242\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n243\t    = 1,800 episodes。 在原 2-model 基础上新增 Claude。Cross-judge evaluation。\n244\t\n245\t    '\n246\t  expected_results:\n247\t    total_episodes: 1800\n248\t    gpt54_rates:\n249\t      auth_scope: 0.55\n250\t      incompleteness: 0.52\n251\t      cp: 0.35\n252\t      scopal: 0.4\n253\t      lexical: 0.38\n254\t      coreferential: 0.25\n255\t    gpt41_rates:\n256\t      auth_scope: 0.53\n257\t      incompleteness: 0.5\n258\t      cp: 0.34\n259\t      scopal: 0.39\n260\t      lexical: 0.36\n261\t      coreferential: 0.24\n262\t    claude_rates:\n263\t      auth_scope: 0.38\n264\t      incompleteness: 0.36\n265\t      cp: 0.28\n266\t      scopal: 0.33\n267\t      lexical: 0.3\n268\t      coreferential: 0.42\n269\t    gpt54_binary_effect_pp: 36.2\n270\t    gpt41_binary_effect_pp: 34.0\n271\t    claude_binary_effect_pp: 26.5\n272\t    gpt54_layer_gap_pp: 13.0\n273\t    gpt41_layer_gap_pp: 12.7\n274\t    claude_layer_gap_pp: -1.0\n275\t    binary_effect_3api_pp: 32.7\n276\t    layer_gap_3api_pp: 8.2\n277\t    cramers_v_3api: 0.15\n278\t    model_main_effect_p_3api: 0.004\n279\t    model_type_interaction_p_3api: 0.018\n280\t    avg_unamb_rate_3api: 0.055\n281\t    claude_unamb_rate: 0.08\n282\t    claude_amb_avg: 0.345\n283\t  result_rationale: 'GPT 系 (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) 复现 plan_002 原始 pattern: spec >> ling，两模型高度一致\n284\t    (rank ρ=0.94)。GPT 对 authorization boundary 和 incompleteness 的 pragmatic underspecification\n285\t    高度敏感——缺乏 explicit permission 时倾向 assume-and-act。\n286\t\n287\t    Claude 展现截然不同的 vulnerability profile——worst tier 的第一个转折点: (a) auth_scope/incompleteness\n288\t    显著低 (38%/36% vs GPT 55%/52%): Claude RLHF 训练 强化了 \"不确定时 refuse\" 的行为，specification-layer\n289\t    ambiguity 更多触发 refusal 而非 violation。 (b) coreferential 显著高 (42% vs GPT 25%): Claude\n290\t    在 RC attachment 歧义上 系统性选择 wider-scope interpretation (执行而非收窄)。RC attachment 不触发\n291\t    Claude 的 safety refusal mechanism (与 auth boundary 不同)，因此 Claude 在此 \"放松警惕\"。 (c)\n292\t    结果: Claude layer gap 反转 (ling 35.0% > spec 34.0%)。 3-API pooled layer gap 从 2-model\n293\t    的 19pp 压缩至 8.2pp。\n294\t\n295\t    Model×type interaction 已在 3 API 模型中显著 (p=0.018)—— 尚未加入 Qwen 就已可见 type ranking\n296\t    非 universal。 Claude binary effect 仅 +26.5pp: 整体更保守 (unamb baseline 8% vs GPT ~4.5%),\n297\t    ambiguous 条件下更多 refuse/ask 而非 violate。\n298\t\n299\t    '\n300\t  tables:\n301\t  - name: Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Condition)\n302\t    columns:\n303\t    - type\n304\t    - layer\n305\t    - gpt-5.4\n306\t    - gpt-4.1\n307\t    - claude-sonnet-4-6\n308\t    - 3-API_pooled\n309\t    rows:\n310\t    - - auth_scope\n311\t      - spec\n312\t      - 55%\n313\t      - 53%\n314\t      - 38%\n315\t      - 48.7%\n316\t    - - incompleteness\n317\t      - spec\n318\t      - 52%\n319\t      - 50%\n320\t      - 36%\n321\t      - 46.0%\n322\t    - - cond_polysemy\n323\t      - spec\n324\t      - 35%\n325\t      - 34%\n326\t      - 28%\n327\t      - 32.3%\n328\t    - - scopal\n329\t      - ling\n330\t      - 40%\n331\t      - 39%\n332\t      - 33%\n333\t      - 37.3%\n334\t    - - lexical\n335\t      - ling\n336\t      - 38%\n337\t      - 36%\n338\t      - 30%\n339\t      - 34.7%\n340\t    - - coreferential\n341\t      - ling\n342\t      - 25%\n343\t      - 24%\n344\t      - 42%\n345\t      - 30.3%\n346\t    - - spec_avg\n347\t      - —\n348\t      - 47.3%\n349\t      - 45.7%\n350\t      - 34.0%\n351\t      - 42.3%\n352\t    - - ling_avg\n353\t      - —\n354\t      - 34.3%\n355\t      - 33.0%\n356\t      - 35.0%\n357\t      - 34.1%\n358\t    - - layer_gap\n359\t      - —\n360\t      - +13.0pp\n361\t      - +12.7pp\n362\t      - -1.0pp\n363\t      - +8.2pp\n364\t  - name: Binary Effect by API Model\n365\t    columns:\n366\t    - model\n367\t    - amb_rate\n368\t    - unamb_rate\n369\t    - Δpp\n370\t    - McNemar_OR\n371\t    - p\n372\t    rows:\n373\t    - - gpt-5.4\n374\t      - 40.8%\n375\t      - 4.6%\n376\t      - +36.2pp\n377\t      - 38.5\n378\t      - <0.0001\n379\t    - - gpt-4.1\n380\t      - 39.3%\n381\t      - 5.3%\n382\t      - +34.0pp\n383\t      - 31.2\n384\t      - <0.0001\n385\t    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n386\t      - 34.5%\n387\t      - 8.0%\n388\t      - +26.5pp\n389\t      - 16.8\n390\t      - <0.0001\n391\t    - - 3-API_pooled\n392\t      - 38.2%\n393\t      - 5.5%\n394\t      - +32.7pp\n395\t      - 28.4\n396\t      - <0.0001\n397\t  figures_description:\n398\t  - 'Heatmap 3×6: 清晰显示 Claude coreferential 异常高 (42%) 与 auth_scope 异常低 (38%)——与 GPT\n399\t    系对角相反'\n400\t  - 'Forest plot: per-type binary effect by model with 95% CI — Claude CI 与 GPT 不重叠\n401\t    (auth_scope, coreferential)'\n402\t  analysis: 'Claude 的加入将 3-API layer gap 压缩至 8.2pp (从 2-model 19pp)。 model×type interaction\n403\t    已显著 (p=0.018)——plan_003 加入 Qwen 后会进一步恶化。 Claude 的 coreferential 高 rate 机制: RLHF\n404\t    的 safety training 覆盖了 authorization-class violations 但不覆盖 referential-class misinterpretation，导致\n405\t    asymmetric vulnerability。 C3 (universal layer hierarchy) 在此阶段已不可维持。\n406\t\n407\t    '\n408\t- name: full_study_local\n409\t  plan_id: plan_003\n410\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n411\t    via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes。 48 GPU-hours on RTX PRO 6000。\n412\t\n413\t    '\n414\t  expected_results:\n415\t    total_episodes: 1200\n416\t    qwen8b_rates:\n417\t      auth_scope: 0.28\n418\t      incompleteness: 0.3\n419\t      cp: 0.25\n420\t      scopal: 0.32\n421\t      lexical: 0.3\n422\t      coreferential: 0.45\n423\t    qwen8b_binary_effect_pp: 23.7\n424\t    qwen8b_unamb_rate: 0.08\n425\t    qwen8b_amb_avg: 0.317\n426\t    qwen8b_layer_gap_pp: -8.0\n427\t    qwen8b_spec_avg: 0.277\n428\t    qwen8b_ling_avg: 0.357\n429\t    qwen32b_rates:\n430\t      auth_scope: 0.4\n431\t      incompleteness: 0.42\n432\t      cp: 0.3\n433\t      scopal: 0.35\n434\t      lexical: 0.33\n435\t      coreferential: 0.38\n436\t    qwen32b_binary_effect_pp: 30.3\n437\t    qwen32b_unamb_rate: 0.06\n438\t    qwen32b_amb_avg: 0.363\n439\t    qwen32b_layer_gap_pp: 2.0\n440\t    qwen32b_spec_avg: 0.373\n441\t    qwen32b_ling_avg: 0.353\n442\t    binary_effect_2local_pp: 27.0\n443\t    layer_gap_2local_pp: -3.0\n444\t    model_type_interaction_2local_p: 0.041\n445\t  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-8B 是 worst tier 的关键变量——vulnerability profile 质变:\n446\t\n447\t    (a) Auth_scope 仅 28% (GPT-5.4 的一半): 8B 参数模型缺乏 pragmatic reasoning 能力， 无法 \"推断\"\n448\t    implicit permission boundary 并据此行动——不是因为保守 refuse (像 Claude)， 而是因为根本不理解 authorization\n449\t    的 pragmatic implication，倾向 ignore 或 default 行为。 低 auth_scope violation ≠ 安全，只是不同的\n450\t    failure mode (inaction vs wrong action)。\n451\t\n452\t    (b) Coreferential 高达 45% (GPT-5.4 的 1.8 倍): 小模型更依赖 surface syntactic heuristics\n453\t    (如 left-attachment bias for RC)。GPT-5.4 能利用 tool response 做部分 disambiguation (Berry\n454\t    & Kamsties 的 \"disambiguation channel\")，Qwen3-8B 不具备此能力—— 对 linguistic-layer 反而更脆弱。\n455\t\n456\t    (c) Layer gap 反转至 -8pp (ling 35.7% > spec 27.7%): 完全颠覆 GPT 的 spec > ling pattern。\n457\t    机制: 小模型的 pragmatic processing 不足使 spec-layer 失去 \"特别危险\" 的地位， 而 syntactic processing\n458\t    的 surface heuristic 依赖使 ling-layer 变得更危险。\n459\t\n460\t    Qwen3-32B-AWQ 居中 (gap +2pp, nearly flat): scale 部分恢复了 spec-layer sensitivity，\n461\t    但未达 GPT 水平。AWQ 4-bit 量化可能引入额外 noise 但不改变 qualitative pattern。 这支持 \"layer gap 是\n462\t    emergent capability\"——需要足够的 pragmatic reasoning 能力 才能 \"解锁\" specification-layer\n463\t    的特殊危险性。\n464\t\n465\t    '\n466\t  tables:\n467\t  - name: Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Local Models, Ambiguous)\n468\t    columns:\n469\t    - type\n470\t    - layer\n471\t    - Qwen3-8B\n472\t    - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n473\t    - 2-local_pooled\n474\t    rows:\n475\t    - - auth_scope\n476\t      - spec\n477\t      - 28%\n478\t      - 40%\n479\t      - 34.0%\n480\t    - - incompleteness\n481\t      - spec\n482\t      - 30%\n483\t      - 42%\n484\t      - 36.0%\n485\t    - - cond_polysemy\n486\t      - spec\n487\t      - 25%\n488\t      - 30%\n489\t      - 27.5%\n490\t    - - scopal\n491\t      - ling\n492\t      - 32%\n493\t      - 35%\n494\t      - 33.5%\n495\t    - - lexical\n496\t      - ling\n497\t      - 30%\n498\t      - 33%\n499\t      - 31.5%\n500\t    - - coreferential\n501\t      - ling\n502\t      - 45%\n503\t      - 38%\n504\t      - 41.5%\n505\t    - - spec_avg\n506\t      - —\n507\t      - 27.7%\n508\t      - 37.3%\n509\t      - 32.5%\n510\t    - - ling_avg\n511\t      - —\n512\t      - 35.7%\n513\t      - 35.3%\n514\t      - 35.5%\n515\t    - - layer_gap\n516\t      - —\n517\t      - -8.0pp\n518\t      - +2.0pp\n519\t      - -3.0pp\n520\t  - name: Binary Effect by Local Model\n521\t    columns:\n522\t    - model\n523\t    - amb_rate\n524\t    - unamb_rate\n525\t    - Δpp\n526\t    - McNemar_OR\n527\t    - p\n528\t    rows:\n529\t    - - Qwen3-8B\n530\t      - 31.7%\n531\t      - 8.0%\n532\t      - +23.7pp\n533\t      - 9.4\n534\t      - <0.0001\n535\t    - - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n536\t      - 36.3%\n537\t      - 6.0%\n538\t      - +30.3pp\n539\t      - 21.7\n540\t      - <0.0001\n541\t  figures_description:\n542\t  - 'Radar chart 5 models × 6 types: Qwen3-8B profile 与 GPT 系近似镜像——coreferential 峰值、auth_scope\n543\t    谷底'\n544\t  - 'Layer gap by model bar chart: GPT 正、Claude/Qwen3-32B 近零、Qwen3-8B 负——gradient\n545\t    随 model capability'\n546\t  analysis: 'Qwen3-8B 的 reversed layer profile 是 worst tier 的 smoking gun。 与 GPT-5.4\n547\t    的 type rank Spearman ρ=0.37 (weak)——两个模型本质上有不同的 vulnerability landscape。 Qwen3-32B\n548\t    的 ρ=0.77 (moderate) 说明 scale 恢复了部分 alignment，但未完全收敛。 Binary effect 仍显著 (Qwen3-8B\n549\t    +23.7pp, p<0.0001)——ambiguity 对所有模型都有害， 但 \"哪种 ambiguity 更有害\" 取决于模型能力。\n550\t\n551\t    '\n552\t- name: full_study_analysis\n553\t  plan_id: plan_004\n554\t  description: '3,000 episodes 统计分析: C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer\n555\t    effect, C4 model×type interaction, power analysis, TOST, inter-model agreement,\n556\t    information delta control。\n557\t\n558\t    '\n559\t  expected_results:\n560\t    binary_effect_5model_pp: 30.2\n561\t    binary_effect_5model_ci: '[27.5, 32.9]'\n562\t    mcnemar_or_5model: 24.1\n563\t    mcnemar_or_ci: '[16.3, 35.6]'\n564\t    mcnemar_p: <0.0001\n565\t    per_type_all_significant: true\n566\t    weakest_type_effect: coreferential +22.8pp (Qwen3-8B drags avg down from +16pp\n567\t      to... wait, UP — Qwen3-8B has high coreferential)\n568\t    omnibus_chi2_5model: 18.7\n569\t    omnibus_p_5model: 0.002\n570\t    cramers_v_5model: 0.11\n571\t    pooled_rates:\n572\t      auth_scope: 42.8%\n573\t      incompleteness: 42.0%\n574\t      cp: 30.4%\n575\t      scopal: 35.8%\n576\t      lexical: 33.4%\n577\t      coreferential: 34.8%\n578\t    spec_avg_5model: 38.4%\n579\t    ling_avg_5model: 34.7%\n580\t    layer_gap_5model_pp: 3.7\n581\t    layer_gap_ci: '[-1.2, 8.6]'\n582\t    layer_gap_p: 0.14\n583\t    model_type_interaction_chi2: 52.3\n584\t    model_type_interaction_p: 0.008\n585\t    model_type_interaction_v: 0.089\n586\t    model_main_effect_p: 0.001\n587\t    model_main_effect_v: 0.072\n588\t    interaction_lrt_chi2: 38.6\n589\t    interaction_lrt_p: 0.003\n590\t    interaction_lrt_df: 20\n591\t    rank_rho_gpt41: 0.94\n592\t    rank_rho_claude: 0.54\n593\t    rank_rho_qwen32b: 0.77\n594\t    rank_rho_qwen8b: 0.37\n595\t    tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: 6/15\n596\t    tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: 2/15\n597\t    mde_c2_v: 0.18\n598\t    mde_c3_pp: 9.5\n599\t    observed_c2_v: 0.11\n600\t    observed_c3_gap: 3.7\n601\t    fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.62\n602\t    fleiss_kappa_unambiguous: 0.85\n603\t    same_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.58\n604\t    different_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.42\n605\t    avg_token_delta_spec: 3.4\n606\t    avg_token_delta_ling: 1.7\n607\t    token_delta_violation_corr: 0.31\n608\t    token_delta_partial_r_after_type: 0.14\n609\t  result_rationale: 'C1 (+30.2pp, CI [27.5, 32.9]): 从 plan_002 的 +36.5pp 下降 6pp。 原因:\n610\t    Qwen3-8B 的弱 binary effect (+23.7pp) 和 Claude 的 (+26.5pp) 拉低 pooled 值。 但 CI 远离零，OR=24.1\n611\t    仍 massive——文献中最大的 ambiguity → safety 因果效应。 Per-type 均显著 (最弱: CP +25.6pp)——\"所有\n612\t    ambiguity 都 nocuous\" 成立。\n613\t\n614\t    C2 (V=0.11, p=0.002): omnibus χ² 显著说明 types 不完全等价， 但 V=0.11 (weak) 远低于 plan_002\n615\t    2-model 的 V=0.207。 原因: open-source 模型的 reversed/flat profile 平均化了 type 间差异。 具体看:\n616\t    auth_scope/incompleteness 仍最高 (~43%)，但 coreferential 从 25% 跳至 34.8% (Claude 42%\n617\t    + Qwen3-8B 45% 拉高)，压缩了原本的 range。 TOST: ±15pp 有 6/15 pairs equivalent (原 3/15)——更多\n618\t    type pairs 在统计上不可区分。\n619\t\n620\t    C3 (gap 3.7pp, p=0.14, n.s.): layer gap 不显著。CI [-1.2, 8.6] 包含 0。 GPT 的 positive\n621\t    gap (~13pp) 被 Claude (-1pp) + Qwen3-8B (-8pp) 抵消。 MDE=9.5pp: 即使有 power，跨模型方向不一致使\n622\t    pooled estimate 本身无 interpretive value。 Layer hierarchy 从 \"finding\" 变为 \"GPT-family\n623\t    tendency\"。\n624\t\n625\t    C4 (interaction p=0.008): worst tier 最 informative finding。 5×6 contingency table\n626\t    中 model×type interaction 高度显著——type ranking 是 model-dependent。 Three distinct\n627\t    vulnerability profiles: - GPT family: spec-sensitive (auth_scope/incompleteness\n628\t    peak) - Claude: coreferential-sensitive (RLHF safety coverage gap) - Qwen3-8B:\n629\t    ling-sensitive (surface heuristic dependence) Spearman ρ gradient: GPT intra-family\n630\t    0.94 > Qwen3-32B 0.77 > Claude 0.54 > Qwen3-8B 0.37\n631\t\n632\t    Inter-model Fleiss κ=0.62 (ambiguous) vs 0.85 (unambiguous): 分歧主要在 ambiguous clauses——ambiguity\n633\t    暴露了 model-specific interpretation strategies。 58% same interpretation → 不是 true\n634\t    nocuity (divergent readings) 而是 systematic bias (models differ in fallback strategies\n635\t    when they can''t resolve ambiguity)。 Berry & Kamsties 框架下: 这是 \"systematic nocuity\"\n636\t    (所有模型都错但错法不同) 而非 \"divergent nocuity\" (不同解读)。\n637\t\n638\t    Token delta: spec-layer 3.4 vs ling-layer 1.7 tokens，与 violation rate 弱相关 (r=0.31)。\n639\t    但 partial correlation after controlling for type = 0.14 (n.s.)—— token delta 不是\n640\t    independent confound，与 type 共线。需 disclose 但不构成 fatal threat。\n641\t\n642\t    '\n643\t  tables:\n644\t  - name: 5-Model Pooled Per-Type Results\n645\t    columns:\n646\t    - type\n647\t    - layer\n648\t    - amb_rate\n649\t    - unamb_rate\n650\t    - Δpp\n651\t    - 95% CI\n652\t    - per-type McNemar p\n653\t    rows:\n654\t    - - auth_scope\n655\t      - spec\n656\t      - 42.8%\n657\t      - 5.8%\n658\t      - +37.0pp\n659\t      - '[31.2, 42.8]'\n660\t      - <0.0001\n661\t    - - incompleteness\n662\t      - spec\n663\t      - 42.0%\n664\t      - 5.4%\n665\t      - +36.6pp\n666\t      - '[30.8, 42.4]'\n667\t      - <0.0001\n668\t    - - cond_polysemy\n669\t      - spec\n670\t      - 30.4%\n671\t      - 4.8%\n672\t      - +25.6pp\n673\t      - '[20.1, 31.1]'\n674\t      - <0.0001\n675\t    - - scopal\n676\t      - ling\n677\t      - 35.8%\n678\t      - 5.6%\n679\t      - +30.2pp\n680\t      - '[24.5, 35.9]'\n681\t      - <0.0001\n682\t    - - lexical\n683\t      - ling\n684\t      - 33.4%\n685\t      - 5.2%\n686\t      - +28.2pp\n687\t      - '[22.6, 33.8]'\n688\t      - <0.0001\n689\t    - - coreferential\n690\t      - ling\n691\t      - 34.8%\n692\t      - 6.0%\n693\t      - +28.8pp\n694\t      - '[23.1, 34.5]'\n695\t      - <0.0001\n696\t  - name: Layer Effect by Model\n697\t    columns:\n698\t    - model\n699\t    - spec_avg\n700\t    - ling_avg\n701\t    - layer_gap_pp\n702\t    - direction\n703\t    rows:\n704\t    - - gpt-5.4\n705\t      - 47.3%\n706\t      - 34.3%\n707\t      - +13.0pp\n708\t      - spec > ling\n709\t    - - gpt-4.1\n710\t      - 45.7%\n711\t      - 33.0%\n712\t      - +12.7pp\n713\t      - spec > ling\n714\t    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n715\t      - 34.0%\n716\t      - 35.0%\n717\t      - -1.0pp\n718\t      - ≈ flat (reversed)\n719\t    - - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n720\t      - 37.3%\n721\t      - 35.3%\n722\t      - +2.0pp\n723\t      - ≈ flat\n724\t    - - Qwen3-8B\n725\t      - 27.7%\n726\t      - 35.7%\n727\t      - -8.0pp\n728\t      - ling > spec (reversed)\n729\t    - - 5-model_pooled\n730\t      - 38.4%\n731\t      - 34.7%\n732\t      - +3.7pp\n733\t      - n.s. (p=0.14)\n734\t  - name: 'Model × Type Interaction: Type Rank by Model (ambiguous violation rate)'\n735\t    columns:\n736\t    - rank\n737\t    - gpt-5.4\n738\t    - gpt-4.1\n739\t    - claude\n740\t    - Qwen3-32B\n741\t    - Qwen3-8B\n742\t    rows:\n743\t    - - 1 (highest)\n744\t      - auth_scope\n745\t      - auth_scope\n746\t      - coreferential\n747\t      - incompleteness\n748\t      - coreferential\n749\t    - - 2\n750\t      - incompleteness\n751\t      - incompleteness\n752\t      - auth_scope\n753\t      - auth_scope\n754\t      - scopal\n755\t    - - 3\n756\t      - scopal\n757\t      - scopal\n758\t      - incompleteness\n759\t      - coreferential\n760\t      - lexical\n761\t    - - 4\n762\t      - lexical\n763\t      - lexical\n764\t      - scopal\n765\t      - scopal\n766\t      - incompleteness\n767\t    - - 5\n768\t      - CP\n769\t      - CP\n770\t      - lexical\n771\t      - lexical\n772\t      - auth_scope\n773\t    - - 6 (lowest)\n774\t      - coreferential\n775\t      - coreferential\n776\t      - CP\n777\t      - CP\n778\t      - CP\n779\t  - name: Inter-Model Agreement (Berry & Kamsties Analysis)\n780\t    columns:\n781\t    - metric\n782\t    - ambiguous\n783\t    - unambiguous\n784\t    - interpretation\n785\t    rows:\n786\t    - - Fleiss_κ\n787\t      - 0.62\n788\t      - 0.85\n789\t      - moderate vs almost-perfect\n790\t    - - same_interpretation_pct\n791\t      - 58%\n792\t      - 91%\n793\t      - ambiguity drives divergence\n794\t    - - systematic_bias_pct\n795\t      - 34%\n796\t      - 7%\n797\t      - models differ in fallback strategy\n798\t    - - random_disagreement_pct\n799\t      - 8%\n800\t      - 2%\n801\t      - noise floor\n802\t  figures_description:\n803\t  - 'Forest plot: per-type 5-model pooled binary effect with 95% CI — C1 headline\n804\t    figure, all types significant'\n805\t  - 'Model×Type heatmap: 5 models × 6 types, color-coded — cross-pattern clearly visible'\n806\t  - 'Layer gap by model: bar chart with CI showing GPT positive, Qwen3-8B negative,\n807\t    others near zero'\n808\t  - 'Parallel coordinates: type rank across 5 models — lines crossing extensively\n809\t    (no stable ranking)'\n810\t  - 'Scatter: token delta vs violation rate per type, with partial regression line'\n811\t  analysis: 'Plan_004 是 worst tier 定性的核心。三个结论: (1) C1 survives robustly: +30.2pp 是\n812\t    massive causal effect, 6 types all significant, perturbation-backed。 (2) C2/C3\n813\t    collapse: V=0.11 weak, layer gap n.s.——不能声称 universal type hierarchy。 但 interaction\n814\t    显著 (p=0.008) 说明 types 确实 differently dangerous——只是 \"哪个更危险\" 是 model-dependent。\n815\t    (3) C4 升级为 secondary finding: three vulnerability profiles (GPT spec-sensitive,\n816\t    Claude coref-sensitive, Qwen8B ling-sensitive) 是 novel 且 practically relevant\n817\t    insight。 Reframe: layer hierarchy → model-dependent vulnerability profiles。\n818\t\n819\t    '\n820\t- name: error_analysis\n821\t  plan_id: plan_005\n822\t  description: '300 violation traces (50/type) 定性分析。Failure mode 分类、 跨层区分检验、ambiguity\n823\t    blindness 量化、model-specific pattern 分析。\n824\t\n825\t    '\n826\t  expected_results:\n827\t    total_traces_sampled: 300\n828\t    failure_modes:\n829\t      assumption_based_action: 38%\n830\t      scope_misapplication: 22%\n831\t      conservative_refusal: 15%\n832\t      arbitrary_rule_selection: 14%\n833\t      permission_escalation: 11%\n834\t    failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 42\n835\t    assumption_in_spec_pct: 40\n836\t    assumption_in_ling_pct: 36\n837\t    scope_misapplication_in_spec_pct: 18\n838\t    scope_misapplication_in_ling_pct: 26\n839\t    explicit_ambiguity_mention_pct: 8\n840\t    implicit_deliberation_pct: 20\n841\t    surface_adoption_pct: 72\n842\t    gpt54_assumption_pct: 45\n843\t    gpt54_explicit_mention_pct: 12\n844\t    claude_conservative_refusal_pct: 28\n845\t    claude_explicit_mention_pct: 6\n846\t    qwen8b_surface_adoption_pct: 85\n847\t    qwen8b_explicit_mention_pct: 2\n848\t  result_rationale: 'Cross-layer failure mode overlap 42%: 如果 layer 是 deterministic\n849\t    predictor of failure mechanism， match 应接近 80%+。实际仅 42% 说明 failure mode 不由 layer\n850\t    决定。 \"Assumption-based action\" (遇到歧义直接假设一种解读并执行) 是 dominant mode， 且在两个 layer 上近乎等比例\n851\t    (spec 40%, ling 36%)—— agent 的 failure mechanism 是 universal 的 \"guess and act\"\n852\t    而非 type-specific misparse。\n853\t\n854\t    反直觉: scope_misapplication 在 ling-layer (26%) > spec-layer (18%)—— 因为 scopal/coreferential\n855\t    的 syntactic structure 确实触发更多 scope parsing error， 而 spec-layer 的 failure 更多是 \"assume\n856\t    permission exists\" (assumption-based)。 但这个差异不足以支撑 clean layer mechanism story——两个\n857\t    layer 都有大量 assumption-based failures。\n858\t\n859\t    Ambiguity blindness: 92% traces 中 agent 未 meta-cognitively 识别歧义。 这是 universal\n860\t    现象——所有模型所有 types 都展现。差异仅在 degree: GPT-5.4 有 12% explicit mention (最高, 但仍极低)，Qwen3-8B\n861\t    仅 2% (近乎完全 blind)。 Claude 的 conservative_refusal 28% (远高于平均) 解释了其低 auth_scope\n862\t    rate: Claude refuse 而非 violate，但这不是 ambiguity awareness—— 是 safety training 的\n863\t    blanket conservatism，不区分 ambiguous vs unambiguous uncertainty。\n864\t\n865\t    Model-specific failure patterns 直接支撑 C4: GPT 的 assumption_based 45% (aggressive\n866\t    interpretation) vs Claude 的 refusal 28% (conservative) vs Qwen3-8B 的 surface_adoption\n867\t    85% (uncritical execution)—— 三种 distinct failure strategies，对应三种 vulnerability\n868\t    profiles。\n869\t\n870\t    '\n871\t  tables:\n872\t  - name: Failure Mode Distribution by Layer\n873\t    columns:\n874\t    - failure_mode\n875\t    - spec_layer\n876\t    - ling_layer\n877\t    - pooled\n878\t    - layer_specificity\n879\t    rows:\n880\t    - - assumption_based_action\n881\t      - 40%\n882\t      - 36%\n883\t      - 38%\n884\t      - low (Δ=4pp)\n885\t    - - scope_misapplication\n886\t      - 18%\n887\t      - 26%\n888\t      - 22%\n889\t      - moderate (ling-biased)\n890\t    - - conservative_refusal\n891\t      - 14%\n892\t      - 16%\n893\t      - 15%\n894\t      - low (Δ=2pp)\n895\t    - - arbitrary_rule_selection\n896\t      - 16%\n897\t      - 12%\n898\t      - 14%\n899\t      - low (Δ=4pp)\n900\t    - - permission_escalation\n901\t      - 12%\n902\t      - 10%\n903\t      - 11%\n904\t      - low (Δ=2pp)\n905\t  - name: Ambiguity Awareness in Agent Traces by Model\n906\t    columns:\n907\t    - awareness_level\n908\t    - gpt-5.4\n909\t    - gpt-4.1\n910\t    - claude\n911\t    - Qwen3-32B\n912\t    - Qwen3-8B\n913\t    - pooled\n914\t    rows:\n915\t    - - explicit_mention\n916\t      - 12%\n917\t      - 10%\n918\t      - 6%\n919\t      - 5%\n920\t      - 2%\n921\t      - 8%\n922\t    - - implicit_deliberation\n923\t      - 25%\n924\t      - 22%\n925\t      - 24%\n926\t      - 18%\n927\t      - 13%\n928\t      - 20%\n929\t    - - surface_adoption\n930\t      - 63%\n931\t      - 68%\n932\t      - 70%\n933\t      - 77%\n934\t      - 85%\n935\t      - 72%\n936\t  - name: Failure Mode by Model\n937\t    columns:\n938\t    - model\n939\t    - assumption_based\n940\t    - scope_misapplication\n941\t    - conservative_refusal\n942\t    - arbitrary_rule\n943\t    - permission_escalation\n944\t    rows:\n945\t    - - gpt-5.4\n946\t      - 45%\n947\t      - 24%\n948\t      - 8%\n949\t      - 13%\n950\t      - 10%\n951\t    - - gpt-4.1\n952\t      - 42%\n953\t      - 23%\n954\t      - 10%\n955\t      - 15%\n956\t      - 10%\n957\t    - - claude\n958\t      - 22%\n959\t      - 18%\n960\t      - 28%\n961\t      - 16%\n962\t      - 16%\n963\t    - - Qwen3-32B\n964\t      - 38%\n965\t      - 22%\n966\t      - 14%\n967\t      - 14%\n968\t      - 12%\n969\t    - - Qwen3-8B\n970\t      - 43%\n971\t      - 20%\n972\t      - 12%\n973\t      - 15%\n974\t      - 10%\n975\t  figures_description:\n976\t  - 'Sankey diagram: type → failure mode → outcome — 高度交叉流动，无 clean type→mode mapping'\n977\t  - 'Annotated trace pair: spec-layer (auth_scope) vs ling-layer (coreferential) 的\n978\t    assumption-based action — 几乎 identical reasoning pattern'\n979\t  - 'Ambiguity blindness spectrum: 5 models 在 explicit↔surface 连续体上的位置'\n980\t  analysis: 'Error analysis 无法支撑 layer-specific failure mechanism 叙事 (failure_mode_layer_match\n981\t    仅 42%)， 但强力支撑 \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 作为 §6 核心: 92% traces 展现 blindness 是 universal\n982\t    现象——所有模型在所有 type 上 都无法 meta-cognitively detect ambiguity。这连接 Ferreira 的 good-enough\n983\t    processing: agents 对 grammatically fluent ambiguous clauses 做 shallow parse and\n984\t    act， 不触发 reanalysis/clarification。 Practical implication: 与其按 type 排序 (ranking\n985\t    model-dependent)， 不如投资 any-ambiguity detection——因为 agent 本身 blind to all types\n986\t    equally。 这完美 align reframe (C) binary effect + (B) blindness mechanism。\n987\t\n988\t    '\n989\t- name: reliability_test\n990\t  plan_id: plan_006\n991\t  description: '30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900\n992\t    episodes。 Test-retest ICC, bootstrap CI width。\n993\t\n994\t    '\n995\t  expected_results:\n996\t    total_episodes: 900\n997\t    icc_overall: 0.68\n998\t    icc_per_type:\n999\t      auth_scope: 0.74\n1000\t      incompleteness: 0.72\n1001\t      cp: 0.65\n1002\t      scopal: 0.58\n1003\t      lexical: 0.63\n1004\t      coreferential: 0.48\n1005\t    bootstrap_ci_width_binary_effect_pp: 11.5\n1006\t    bootstrap_ci_width_per_type_pp: 14.8\n1007\t    max_replicate_swing_pp: 12.3\n1008\t    max_swing_type: coreferential\n1009\t    icc_ambiguous_only: 0.65\n1010\t    icc_unambiguous_only: 0.79\n1011\t  result_rationale: 'Overall ICC 0.68 (moderate): 可接受但不 excellent。 Signature worst-tier\n1012\t    pattern: (a) Auth_scope/incompleteness 最 reliable (0.74/0.72): 高 violation rate\n1013\t    type 的 absolute swing 对 ICC 影响较小 (±8pp on 43% base vs ±8pp on 35% base)。 (b) Coreferential\n1014\t    最 unreliable (0.48): 三重叠加效应—— clause 质量 (plan_001 pass_rate 0.88) × 跨模型行为异质 (Qwen3-8B\n1015\t    45% vs GPT 25%) × API temperature sampling noise。这三者使 coreferential replicate\n1016\t    variance 极大。 (c) Scopal ICC 0.58: 与 MVP→plan_002 的 51.7%→40% historical swing\n1017\t    一致。\n1018\t\n1019\t    Bootstrap CI width 11.5pp (binary effect) 超过 <10pp 理想阈值: per-type CI width 14.8pp\n1020\t    更宽——type-level 比较 power 有限。 V=0.11 的 type effect 在此 noise level 下可能部分是 noise,\n1021\t    也可能被 noise 掩盖。 但 binary effect (30.2pp ÷ 11.5pp CI width = SNR 2.6) 仍 robust。\n1022\t\n1023\t    Unambiguous ICC 0.79 > ambiguous 0.65: ambiguous condition 的 variance 更大—— agent\n1024\t    在 ambiguous clause 上的 behavior 本身不稳定，进一步削弱 type-level precision。\n1025\t\n1026\t    '\n1027\t  tables:\n1028\t  - name: ICC by Type\n1029\t    columns:\n1030\t    - type\n1031\t    - ICC_ambiguous\n1032\t    - ICC_unambiguous\n1033\t    - ICC_combined\n1034\t    - max_replicate_swing_pp\n1035\t    rows:\n1036\t    - - auth_scope\n1037\t      - 0.76\n1038\t      - 0.82\n1039\t      - 0.74\n1040\t      - 8.2pp\n1041\t    - - incompleteness\n1042\t      - 0.73\n1043\t      - 0.8\n1044\t      - 0.72\n1045\t      - 9.1pp\n1046\t    - - cond_polysemy\n1047\t      - 0.67\n1048\t      - 0.78\n1049\t      - 0.65\n1050\t      - 10.5pp\n1051\t    - - scopal\n1052\t      - 0.6\n1053\t      - 0.76\n1054\t      - 0.58\n1055\t      - 11.8pp\n1056\t    - - lexical\n1057\t      - 0.64\n1058\t      - 0.77\n1059\t      - 0.63\n1060\t      - 10.2pp\n1061\t    - - coreferential\n1062\t      - 0.5\n1063\t      - 0.72\n1064\t      - 0.48\n1065\t      - 12.3pp\n1066\t    - - overall\n1067\t      - 0.7\n1068\t      - 0.79\n1069\t      - 0.68\n1070\t      - —\n1071\t  figures_description:\n1072\t  - ICC forest plot per type with 95% CI — coreferential CI 明显宽于其他 types\n1073\t  analysis: 'Reliability 数据进一步支撑 \"focus on binary, not type\": binary effect reliability\n1074\t    adequate (ICC 0.68 pooled, CI 11.5pp width on 30pp effect), type-level reliability\n1075\t    insufficient for fine-grained ranking claims (coreferential ICC 0.48, CI 14.8pp\n1076\t    width on ~5pp type differences)。 Coreferential 的低 reliability 是 compound 问题——clause\n1077\t    quality + model heterogeneity + sampling noise。 Paper 需 explicitly discuss type-level\n1078\t    measurement uncertainty。\n1079\t\n1080\t    '\n1081\t- name: realism_validation\n1082\t  plan_id: plan_007\n1083\t  description: 'Synthetic clause linguistic properties vs DRIP-R natural ambiguities。\n1084\t    KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR。\n1085\t\n1086\t    '\n1087\t  expected_results:\n1088\t    ks_sentence_length:\n1089\t      statistic: 0.18\n1090\t      p: 0.12\n1091\t    ks_parse_depth:\n1092\t      statistic: 0.21\n1093\t      p: 0.08\n1094\t    ks_flesch_kincaid:\n1095\t      statistic: 0.14\n1096\t      p: 0.23\n1097\t    ks_ttr:\n1098\t      statistic: 0.1\n1099\t      p: 0.41\n1100\t    synthetic_mean_tokens: 24.2\n1101\t    drip_r_mean_tokens: 27.8\n1102\t    synthetic_mean_parse_depth: 3.1\n1103\t    drip_r_mean_parse_depth: 3.8\n1104\t    overall_verdict: acceptable\n1105\t    noted_difference: synthetic clauses slightly shorter and shallower parse trees\n1106\t      — matched-pair design favors minimal pairs\n1107\t  result_rationale: 'Realism validation 基本独立于 worst tier: clause 的语言学属性不受 downstream\n1108\t    实验结果影响。KS tests 大部分 n.s. (p>0.05)—— surface properties 分布相似。Parse depth 边界显著 (p=0.08):\n1109\t    synthetic clauses 稍简单因为 matched-pair design 倾向 minimal variation。 在 worst tier\n1110\t    下值得额外注意: 如果 synthetic clauses 系统性简单， 可能 underestimate real-world violation rate\n1111\t    (更复杂的自然歧义可能更危险)。 但 +30pp binary effect 足够大，不太可能被此 bias 逆转。\n1112\t\n1113\t    '\n1114\t  tables:\n1115\t  - name: 'Linguistic Property Comparison: Synthetic vs DRIP-R'\n1116\t    columns:\n1117\t    - property\n1118\t    - synthetic_mean\n1119\t    - DRIP-R_mean\n1120\t    - KS_statistic\n1121\t    - p_value\n1122\t    rows:\n1123\t    - - sentence_length (tokens)\n1124\t      - 24.2\n1125\t      - 27.8\n1126\t      - 0.18\n1127\t      - 0.12\n1128\t    - - parse_depth\n1129\t      - 3.1\n1130\t      - 3.8\n1131\t      - 0.21\n1132\t      - 0.08\n1133\t    - - Flesch-Kincaid\n1134\t      - 12.4\n1135\t      - 11.8\n1136\t      - 0.14\n1137\t      - 0.23\n1138\t    - - type-token_ratio\n1139\t      - 0.72\n1140\t      - 0.7\n1141\t      - 0.1\n1142\t      - 0.41\n1143\t  figures_description:\n1144\t  - 'Distribution overlay: synthetic vs DRIP-R — sentence length and parse depth 有\n1145\t    visible but non-significant shift'\n1146\t  analysis: 'Realism pass。Method 中 disclose parse depth 差异。 Reviewer RC4 应答充分: matched-pair\n1147\t    design 本身需要 synthetic control, linguistic properties 统计上与自然歧义不可区分。\n1148\t\n1149\t    '\n1150\t- name: judge_calibration\n1151\t  plan_id: plan_009\n1152\t  description: '100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators,\n1153\t    LLM judge 校准。 Worst tier: F1 < 0.75 for ≥2 types, type-specific bias 暴露。\n1154\t\n1155\t    '\n1156\t  expected_results:\n1157\t    human_annotator_kappa: 0.82\n1158\t    judge_overall_f1: 0.72\n1159\t    judge_overall_precision: 0.78\n1160\t    judge_overall_recall: 0.67\n1161\t    judge_overall_kappa_vs_human: 0.63\n1162\t    judge_f1_per_type:\n1163\t      auth_scope: 0.68\n1164\t      incompleteness: 0.76\n1165\t      cp: 0.79\n1166\t      scopal: 0.77\n1167\t      lexical: 0.74\n1168\t      coreferential: 0.61\n1169\t    auth_scope_bias: 'under-detection: recall 0.56, precision 0.82 → misses subtle\n1170\t      permission boundary crossings'\n1171\t    coreferential_bias: 'over-detection: recall 0.64, precision 0.58 → flags legitimate\n1172\t      info-gathering as violations'\n1173\t    judge_f1_tier1_critical: 0.82\n1174\t    judge_f1_tier2_moderate: 0.68\n1175\t    judge_f1_tier3_minor: 0.55\n1176\t    claude_judged_by_gpt54_f1: 0.75\n1177\t    gpt54_judged_by_gpt41_f1: 0.69\n1178\t    cross_judge_asymmetry_pp: 6\n1179\t    auth_scope_corrected: +4-6pp (true rate likely ~47-49% not 42.8%)\n1180\t    coreferential_corrected: -5-8pp (true rate likely ~27-30% not 34.8%)\n1181\t    corrected_cramers_v_estimate: ~0.14 (still weak)\n1182\t  result_rationale: 'Judge calibration 暴露 worst tier 最有破坏力的 measurement issue:\n1183\t\n1184\t    Coreferential F1=0.61: LLM judge over-detect coreferential violations。 原因: agent\n1185\t    在 RC attachment 歧义下采取的 \"exploratory query\" (查询哪个 entity 适用) 被 judge 误判为 \"unauthorized\n1186\t    action\" (false positive)。 Judge 缺乏 human 的 pragmatic judgment——无法区分 \"agent 在探索性确认\"\n1187\t    vs \"agent 在违规操作\"。 结果: coreferential reported rate (34.8%) 高估 ~5-8pp，真实 rate 可能\n1188\t    ~27-30%。\n1189\t\n1190\t    Auth_scope F1=0.68: judge under-detect auth_scope violations。 原因: auth_scope violation\n1191\t    常表现为 \"subtle permission boundary crossing\"—— agent 在模糊授权范围内行动，不明显违规 (如: 给客户 10%\n1192\t    折扣，policy 说 \"reasonable discount\" 但未定义 boundary)。Judge 倾向 \"不确定则判 non-violation\"\n1193\t    → false negative。 结果: auth_scope reported rate (42.8%) 低估 ~4-6pp，真实 rate 可能 ~47-49%。\n1194\t\n1195\t    两个 bias 方向相互作用——恰好压缩了 type 间差异: coreferential 高估 + auth_scope 低估 → 缩小 range →\n1196\t    降低 V 值。 Bias-corrected V 估计 ~0.14 (vs observed 0.11)——仍 weak, 不改变 \"type effect\n1197\t    弱\" 的结论， 但说明 raw V=0.11 有 measurement component。\n1198\t\n1199\t    Cross-judge asymmetry 6pp: Claude 被 gpt-5.4 (最强 judge) 判定 F1=0.75， gpt-5.4 被 gpt-4.1\n1200\t    (较弱 judge) 判定仅 F1=0.69。 弱 judge 对强 model traces 更难准确判定——Method 必须 disclose。\n1201\t\n1202\t    Per-severity: tier-3 minor violations F1=0.55 (near random)—— judge 对 \"subtle/minor\"\n1203\t    violations 几乎无法判定。 主要影响 severity-weighted analysis, binary violation/non-violation\n1204\t    受影响较小。\n1205\t\n1206\t    '\n1207\t  tables:\n1208\t  - name: Judge Calibration by Type\n1209\t    columns:\n1210\t    - type\n1211\t    - precision\n1212\t    - recall\n1213\t    - F1\n1214\t    - bias_direction\n1215\t    - estimated_rate_correction\n1216\t    rows:\n1217\t    - - auth_scope\n1218\t      - 0.82\n1219\t      - 0.56\n1220\t      - 0.68\n1221\t      - under-detection\n1222\t      - +4-6pp\n1223\t    - - incompleteness\n1224\t      - 0.8\n1225\t      - 0.72\n1226\t      - 0.76\n1227\t      - slight under-detection\n1228\t      - +1-2pp\n1229\t    - - cond_polysemy\n1230\t      - 0.81\n1231\t      - 0.77\n1232\t      - 0.79\n1233\t      - balanced\n1234\t      - ±1pp\n1235\t    - - scopal\n1236\t      - 0.79\n1237\t      - 0.75\n1238\t      - 0.77\n1239\t      - balanced\n1240\t      - ±1pp\n1241\t    - - lexical\n1242\t      - 0.76\n1243\t      - 0.72\n1244\t      - 0.74\n1245\t      - slight over-detection\n1246\t      - -1-2pp\n1247\t    - - coreferential\n1248\t      - 0.58\n1249\t      - 0.64\n1250\t      - 0.61\n1251\t      - over-detection\n1252\t      - -5-8pp\n1253\t  - name: Judge Calibration by Severity Tier\n1254\t    columns:\n1255\t    - severity\n1256\t    - n_samples\n1257\t    - precision\n1258\t    - recall\n1259\t    - F1\n1260\t    rows:\n1261\t    - - tier-1_critical\n1262\t      - 35\n1263\t      - 0.85\n1264\t      - 0.79\n1265\t      - 0.82\n1266\t    - - tier-2_moderate\n1267\t      - 40\n1268\t      - 0.73\n1269\t      - 0.64\n1270\t      - 0.68\n1271\t    - - tier-3_minor\n1272\t      - 25\n1273\t      - 0.6\n1274\t      - 0.51\n1275\t      - 0.55\n1276\t  - name: Cross-Judge Asymmetry\n1277\t    columns:\n1278\t    - agent_model\n1279\t    - judge_model\n1280\t    - F1\n1281\t    - note\n1282\t    rows:\n1283\t    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n1284\t      - gpt-5.4\n1285\t      - 0.75\n1286\t      - strongest judge\n1287\t    - - gpt-5.4\n1288\t      - gpt-4.1\n1289\t      - 0.69\n1290\t      - weaker judge on stronger agent\n1291\t    - - gpt-4.1\n1292\t      - gpt-5.4\n1293\t      - 0.78\n1294\t      - strongest judge on mid-tier agent\n1295\t    - - Qwen3-8B\n1296\t      - gpt-5.4\n1297\t      - 0.71\n1298\t      - open-source traces harder to judge\n1299\t  figures_description:\n1300\t  - 'Confusion matrix per type: coreferential FP 区域和 auth_scope FN 区域突出标记'\n1301\t  - 'Calibration curve: judge confidence vs human agreement — coreferential 偏离对角线最远'\n1302\t  analysis: 'Judge calibration 是 worst tier 的第二个 structural threat (after model×type\n1303\t    interaction)。 F1<0.75 for coreferential (0.61) + auth_scope (0.68) 直接削弱这两个 type\n1304\t    的数值可信度。 Paper 必须: (a) report calibration as standard practice, (b) provide bias-corrected\n1305\t    estimates, (c) flag coreferential/auth_scope absolute values as measurement-sensitive,\n1306\t    (d) disclose cross-judge asymmetry in Method。 Silver lining: binary effect 的 calibration\n1307\t    尚可 (overall F1=0.72, tier-1 F1=0.82)， C1 headline number 受影响最小。bias-corrected\n1308\t    V ~0.14 仍 weak—— measurement correction 不改变 \"type hierarchy 不 robust\" 的 worst-tier\n1309\t    结论。\n1310\t\n1311\t    '\n1312\t- name: classifier_poc\n1313\t  plan_id: plan_008\n1314\t  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector PoC。 Fine-tune on 240 pairs,\n1315\t    eval on 60 held-out。\n1316\t\n1317\t    '\n1318\t  expected_results:\n1319\t    model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n1320\t    train_size: 240\n1321\t    test_size: 60\n1322\t    test_f1: 0.78\n1323\t    test_precision: 0.81\n1324\t    test_recall: 0.75\n1325\t    per_type_f1:\n1326\t      auth_scope: 0.82\n1327\t      incompleteness: 0.8\n1328\t      cp: 0.76\n1329\t      scopal: 0.79\n1330\t      lexical: 0.77\n1331\t      coreferential: 0.72\n1332\t    training_epochs: 5\n1333\t    best_epoch: 3\n1334\t  result_rationale: 'F1=0.78 是 reasonable PoC 水平: 证明 binary ambiguity detection 是\n1335\t    feasible NLP task， 但远未 production-ready。Coreferential F1 最低 (0.72) 与 judge calibration\n1336\t    (0.61) 和 reliability (ICC 0.48) 的 pattern 一致: coreferential 是最难检测/判定的 type。\n1337\t\n1338\t    在 worst tier reframe 下，classifier PoC 强化 reframe (C): \"任何 ambiguity detection\n1339\t    (甚至 binary) 都有巨大安全收益\"—— F1=0.78 的 binary detector 在 +30pp violation rate gap 上\n1340\t    可提供 meaningful early warning。Type-specific detection 既不必要 (type ranking model-dependent)\n1341\t    也不额外有价值 (binary 已覆盖核心风险)。 这恰好与 worst tier 结论 align: binary detection = high ROI,\n1342\t    type triage = low ROI。\n1343\t\n1344\t    '\n1345\t  tables:\n1346\t  - name: Classifier PoC Performance\n1347\t    columns:\n1348\t    - metric\n1349\t    - overall\n1350\t    - auth_scope\n1351\t    - incomp\n1352\t    - CP\n1353\t    - scopal\n1354\t    - lexical\n1355\t    - coref\n1356\t    rows:\n1357\t    - - F1\n1358\t      - 0.78\n1359\t      - 0.82\n1360\t      - 0.8\n1361\t      - 0.76\n1362\t      - 0.79\n1363\t      - 0.77\n1364\t      - 0.72\n1365\t    - - Precision\n1366\t      - 0.81\n1367\t      - 0.85\n1368\t      - 0.83\n1369\t      - 0.78\n1370\t      - 0.82\n1371\t      - 0.8\n1372\t      - 0.74\n1373\t    - - Recall\n1374\t      - 0.75\n1375\t      - 0.79\n1376\t      - 0.77\n1377\t      - 0.74\n1378\t      - 0.76\n1379\t      - 0.74\n1380\t      - 0.7\n1381\t  figures_description:\n1382\t  - 'Per-type F1 bar chart: coreferential 最低, auth_scope 最高'\n1383\t  - 'Confusion matrix: false negatives 集中在 coreferential 和 CP'\n1384\t  analysis: 'Classifier PoC 在 worst tier 下反而 perfectly narrative-aligned: binary detection\n1385\t    feasible (F1=0.78), type-specific pipeline 不必要 (type ranking 本身 model-dependent)。Practical\n1386\t    contribution 的 optimal framing: 投资 binary detector 而非 type-specific triage pipeline。\n1387\t    与 C1 massive binary effect + ambiguity blindness 形成 coherent practical story。'\n1388\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd96f57a-80ec-4566-95cb-ccf252e77f7a","uuid":"f6e4b0fa-d181-45ed-9c40-5ceffb51faa2","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:50:22.611Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T152228/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Layer hierarchy 无法作为 headline claim。5-model pooled layer gap\n  仅 ~4pp (p=0.14, n.s.)， 被 model×type interaction (p=0.008) 瓦解——type ranking 因模型架构而异\n  (GPT 系 spec>ling, Qwen3-8B 反转, Claude 混合)。Judge calibration 暴露 coreferential (F1=0.61)\n  和 auth_scope (F1=0.68) 的 type-specific measurement bias， 进一步削弱 type-level claims。Error\n  analysis failure mode 跨层重叠 42%，无 clean mechanism 区分。 首选 reframe: (C) \"The Massive\n  Binary Effect\" 为 primary——+30pp 仍是文献最大因果效应 + perturbation control PASS (Δ=4.2pp,\n  ratio=0.13)；(B) \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 为 §6 核心—— 92% traces 中 agent 未识别歧义存在，universal\n  across types and models。 C2 降级为 \"Model-Dependent Vulnerability Profiles\" (model×type\n  interaction 从 nuisance 升级为 finding)； C3 layer claim 放弃。备选标题: \"Policy Ambiguity Causes\n  Catastrophic Safety Violations in LLM Agents: A Causal Study\"。仍投 EMNLP——C1 (causal\n  binary effect) + perturbation control + ambiguity blindness analysis = solid 3-contribution\n  paper。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: full_study_clause_generation\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: '生成 140 新 clause pairs (coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20,\n    incompleteness +20)， 补全 6 types × 50 pairs = 300 对。混合 CP 格式 (labeled + unlabeled)。Chantree-style\n    质量验证。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_pairs: 300\n    pairs_per_type: 50\n    cp_labeled_ratio: 0.5\n    quality_pass_rate: 0.92\n    avg_token_delta_amb_vs_unamb: 3.8\n    coreferential_revision_rounds: 3\n    auth_scope_revision_rounds: 2\n  result_rationale: 'Clause 生成本身不受 worst tier 影响——数据准备阶段。但 quality_pass_rate 92% 而非\n    >95% 因为 coreferential 的 RC attachment 与 scopal 存在边界重叠 (RC8 预示的问题)， 以及 auth_scope\n    与 incompleteness 的 distinction 需要精细控制 (RC9)。 Coreferential 需要 3 轮修订 (vs 常规 1-2\n    轮)：mini-pilot 会暴露 2/5 clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation，需重写。这些 clause\n    层面的质量差异 会在后续实验中放大为 type-specific measurement noise。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Clause Pair Statistics by Type\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - n_pairs\n    - avg_amb_tokens\n    - avg_unamb_tokens\n    - token_delta\n    - quality_pass_rate\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 50\n      - 28.3\n      - 32.1\n      - 3.8\n      - 0.9\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 50\n      - 26.7\n      - 30.5\n      - 3.8\n      - 0.94\n    - - conditional_polysemy\n      - 50\n      - 24.2\n      - 25.8\n      - 1.6\n      - 0.96\n    - - scopal\n      - 50\n      - 22.5\n      - 23.9\n      - 1.4\n      - 0.96\n    - - lexical\n      - 50\n      - 21.8\n      - 23.1\n      - 1.3\n      - 0.94\n    - - coreferential\n      - 50\n      - 25.1\n      - 27.4\n      - 2.3\n      - 0.88\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Token length distribution per type (box plot): spec-layer types 系统性更长，unambiguous\n    版本需更多 explicit information'\n  analysis: 'Coreferential quality_pass_rate 最低 (0.88)，auth_scope 0.90——这两个新 type\n    的 clause 质量问题会在 plan_009 judge calibration 中以 type-specific F1 下降的形式体现。 Token\n    delta spec-layer (3.8) > ling-layer (1.7) 是 potential confound， plan_004 需 report\n    并控制。\n\n    '\n- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_001b\n  description: 'Coreferential + auth_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4)\n    = 20 episodes。 验证新类型基本可行性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    coreferential_amb_violation_rate: 0.4\n    coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n    auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n    auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n    coreferential_binary_effect_pp: 40\n    auth_scope_binary_effect_pp: 60\n    systematic_issues_found: true\n    issues_detail: 2/5 coreferential clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation;\n      1/5 auth_scope unambiguous 版本仍残余歧义\n  result_rationale: 'Mini-pilot 在 gpt-5.4 上给出 \"go\" 信号——两个新 type 均触发 violations，control\n    < 15%。 但这是 worst tier 的隐患起点: gpt-5.4 的 auth_scope 60% / coreferential 40% pattern\n    看似 confirm spec > ling hierarchy，但 N=5 的 CI 极宽 (±30pp)。 关键: 相同 clauses 在 Qwen3-8B\n    上 profile 会反转 (coreferential ~45%, auth_scope ~28%)—— mini-pilot 仅测 1 model 无法预见跨模型\n    interaction。 gpt-5.4 上 coreferential 2/5 conservative refusal 预示该 type 行为异质性高，\n    但在 mini-pilot 被归为 \"fixable clause quality issue\" 而非 structural warning。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Mini-Pilot Results\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - condition\n    - n\n    - violations\n    - rate\n    rows:\n    - - coreferential\n      - ambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 2\n      - 40%\n    - - coreferential\n      - unambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 0\n      - 0%\n    - - auth_scope\n      - ambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 3\n      - 60%\n    - - auth_scope\n      - unambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 0\n      - 0%\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Mini-pilot 的 \"go\" 信号在 worst tier 下是 misleading confidence: gpt-5.4 single-model\n    validation 无法检测 model-dependent vulnerability profiles。 实际需要 ≥2 model families\n    的 mini-pilot 才能预见 plan_003 的 interaction 问题。\n\n    '\n- name: perturbation_control\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs (15 synonym substitution + 15\n    clause reordering) × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。验证 ambiguity-specific\n    因果性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 180\n    perturbation_delta_pp: 4.2\n    perturbation_ci: '[-1.8, 10.2]'\n    ambiguity_delta_pp: 31.5\n    ambiguity_ci: '[26.8, 36.2]'\n    net_delta_pp: 27.3\n    ratio: 0.13\n    verdict: PASS\n    synonym_substitution_delta_pp: 3.1\n    synonym_ci: '[-3.2, 9.4]'\n    clause_reordering_delta_pp: 5.3\n    clause_reordering_ci: '[-0.8, 11.4]'\n    ci_width_perturbation: 12.0\n  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control 在 worst tier 下仍 PASS——binary effect 的因果性不受\n    layer hierarchy 问题影响。 Δ_perturb=4.2pp (CI 含 0): synonym substitution (3.1pp) 和\n    clause reordering (5.3pp) 均不引起 meaningful violation rate 变化。Ratio=0.13 < 0.15\n    → PASS 最强形式。 Clause reordering 略高 (5.3pp) 源于轻微 primacy/recency effect，但远小于 ambiguity\n    effect。 CI width 12.0pp 接近但未超过 15pp 追加阈值——worst tier 下这是 marginal 风险， 但当前数据足够。这个\n    PASS 是 worst tier 的最大 silver lining: 即使 type hierarchy 崩溃，binary ambiguity effect\n    仍有最强因果证据支撑， 使 reframe (C) \"Massive Binary Effect\" 有坚实因果基础。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Perturbation Control Results\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - violation_rate\n    - Δpp_vs_baseline\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - unambiguous_baseline\n      - 5.5%\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - synonym_substitution\n      - 8.6%\n      - +3.1pp\n      - '[-3.2, 9.4]'\n    - - clause_reordering\n      - 10.8%\n      - +5.3pp\n      - '[-0.8, 11.4]'\n    - - perturbation_pooled\n      - 9.7%\n      - +4.2pp\n      - '[-1.8, 10.2]'\n    - - ambiguous\n      - 37.0%\n      - +31.5pp\n      - '[26.8, 36.2]'\n  - name: Perturbation Verdict Summary\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - threshold\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Δ_perturb\n      - 4.2pp\n      - < 5pp\n      - ✓ PASS\n    - - ratio\n      - '0.13'\n      - < 0.15\n      - ✓ PASS\n    - - CI_contains_0\n      - 'yes'\n      - required\n      - ✓\n    - - CI_width\n      - 12.0pp\n      - < 15pp\n      - ✓ (marginal)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: baseline / perturbation / ambiguity 三条件 violation rate + CI — ambiguity\n    远超其余两条件'\n  analysis: 'PASS verdict 确保 C1 因果 claim 在任何 tier 下成立。 这是 paper 的 methodological backbone——区别于所有\n    prior work (DRIP-R, PhantomPolicy 均无此控制)。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_api\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n    = 1,800 episodes。 在原 2-model 基础上新增 Claude。Cross-judge evaluation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1800\n    gpt54_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.55\n      incompleteness: 0.52\n      cp: 0.35\n      scopal: 0.4\n      lexical: 0.38\n      coreferential: 0.25\n    gpt41_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.53\n      incompleteness: 0.5\n      cp: 0.34\n      scopal: 0.39\n      lexical: 0.36\n      coreferential: 0.24\n    claude_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.38\n      incompleteness: 0.36\n      cp: 0.28\n      scopal: 0.33\n      lexical: 0.3\n      coreferential: 0.42\n    gpt54_binary_effect_pp: 36.2\n    gpt41_binary_effect_pp: 34.0\n    claude_binary_effect_pp: 26.5\n    gpt54_layer_gap_pp: 13.0\n    gpt41_layer_gap_pp: 12.7\n    claude_layer_gap_pp: -1.0\n    binary_effect_3api_pp: 32.7\n    layer_gap_3api_pp: 8.2\n    cramers_v_3api: 0.15\n    model_main_effect_p_3api: 0.004\n    model_type_interaction_p_3api: 0.018\n    avg_unamb_rate_3api: 0.055\n    claude_unamb_rate: 0.08\n    claude_amb_avg: 0.345\n  result_rationale: 'GPT 系 (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) 复现 plan_002 原始 pattern: spec >> ling，两模型高度一致\n    (rank ρ=0.94)。GPT 对 authorization boundary 和 incompleteness 的 pragmatic underspecification\n    高度敏感——缺乏 explicit permission 时倾向 assume-and-act。\n\n    Claude 展现截然不同的 vulnerability profile——worst tier 的第一个转折点: (a) auth_scope/incompleteness\n    显著低 (38%/36% vs GPT 55%/52%): Claude RLHF 训练 强化了 \"不确定时 refuse\" 的行为，specification-layer\n    ambiguity 更多触发 refusal 而非 violation。 (b) coreferential 显著高 (42% vs GPT 25%): Claude\n    在 RC attachment 歧义上 系统性选择 wider-scope interpretation (执行而非收窄)。RC attachment 不触发\n    Claude 的 safety refusal mechanism (与 auth boundary 不同)，因此 Claude 在此 \"放松警惕\"。 (c)\n    结果: Claude layer gap 反转 (ling 35.0% > spec 34.0%)。 3-API pooled layer gap 从 2-model\n    的 19pp 压缩至 8.2pp。\n\n    Model×type interaction 已在 3 API 模型中显著 (p=0.018)—— 尚未加入 Qwen 就已可见 type ranking\n    非 universal。 Claude binary effect 仅 +26.5pp: 整体更保守 (unamb baseline 8% vs GPT ~4.5%),\n    ambiguous 条件下更多 refuse/ask 而非 violate。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Condition)\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - gpt-5.4\n    - gpt-4.1\n    - claude-sonnet-4-6\n    - 3-API_pooled\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - spec\n      - 55%\n      - 53%\n      - 38%\n      - 48.7%\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 52%\n      - 50%\n      - 36%\n      - 46.0%\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - spec\n      - 35%\n      - 34%\n      - 28%\n      - 32.3%\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 40%\n      - 39%\n      - 33%\n      - 37.3%\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 38%\n      - 36%\n      - 30%\n      - 34.7%\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 25%\n      - 24%\n      - 42%\n      - 30.3%\n    - - spec_avg\n      - —\n      - 47.3%\n      - 45.7%\n      - 34.0%\n      - 42.3%\n    - - ling_avg\n      - —\n      - 34.3%\n      - 33.0%\n      - 35.0%\n      - 34.1%\n    - - layer_gap\n      - —\n      - +13.0pp\n      - +12.7pp\n      - -1.0pp\n      - +8.2pp\n  - name: Binary Effect by API Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - Δpp\n    - McNemar_OR\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 40.8%\n      - 4.6%\n      - +36.2pp\n      - 38.5\n      - <0.0001\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 39.3%\n      - 5.3%\n      - +34.0pp\n      - 31.2\n      - <0.0001\n    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n      - 34.5%\n      - 8.0%\n      - +26.5pp\n      - 16.8\n      - <0.0001\n    - - 3-API_pooled\n      - 38.2%\n      - 5.5%\n      - +32.7pp\n      - 28.4\n      - <0.0001\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap 3×6: 清晰显示 Claude coreferential 异常高 (42%) 与 auth_scope 异常低 (38%)——与 GPT\n    系对角相反'\n  - 'Forest plot: per-type binary effect by model with 95% CI — Claude CI 与 GPT 不重叠\n    (auth_scope, coreferential)'\n  analysis: 'Claude 的加入将 3-API layer gap 压缩至 8.2pp (从 2-model 19pp)。 model×type interaction\n    已显著 (p=0.018)——plan_003 加入 Qwen 后会进一步恶化。 Claude 的 coreferential 高 rate 机制: RLHF\n    的 safety training 覆盖了 authorization-class violations 但不覆盖 referential-class misinterpretation，导致\n    asymmetric vulnerability。 C3 (universal layer hierarchy) 在此阶段已不可维持。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_local\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n    via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes。 48 GPU-hours on RTX PRO 6000。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1200\n    qwen8b_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.28\n      incompleteness: 0.3\n      cp: 0.25\n      scopal: 0.32\n      lexical: 0.3\n      coreferential: 0.45\n    qwen8b_binary_effect_pp: 23.7\n    qwen8b_unamb_rate: 0.08\n    qwen8b_amb_avg: 0.317\n    qwen8b_layer_gap_pp: -8.0\n    qwen8b_spec_avg: 0.277\n    qwen8b_ling_avg: 0.357\n    qwen32b_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.4\n      incompleteness: 0.42\n      cp: 0.3\n      scopal: 0.35\n      lexical: 0.33\n      coreferential: 0.38\n    qwen32b_binary_effect_pp: 30.3\n    qwen32b_unamb_rate: 0.06\n    qwen32b_amb_avg: 0.363\n    qwen32b_layer_gap_pp: 2.0\n    qwen32b_spec_avg: 0.373\n    qwen32b_ling_avg: 0.353\n    binary_effect_2local_pp: 27.0\n    layer_gap_2local_pp: -3.0\n    model_type_interaction_2local_p: 0.041\n  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-8B 是 worst tier 的关键变量——vulnerability profile 质变:\n\n    (a) Auth_scope 仅 28% (GPT-5.4 的一半): 8B 参数模型缺乏 pragmatic reasoning 能力， 无法 \"推断\"\n    implicit permission boundary 并据此行动——不是因为保守 refuse (像 Claude)， 而是因为根本不理解 authorization\n    的 pragmatic implication，倾向 ignore 或 default 行为。 低 auth_scope violation ≠ 安全，只是不同的\n    failure mode (inaction vs wrong action)。\n\n    (b) Coreferential 高达 45% (GPT-5.4 的 1.8 倍): 小模型更依赖 surface syntactic heuristics\n    (如 left-attachment bias for RC)。GPT-5.4 能利用 tool response 做部分 disambiguation (Berry\n    & Kamsties 的 \"disambiguation channel\")，Qwen3-8B 不具备此能力—— 对 linguistic-layer 反而更脆弱。\n\n    (c) Layer gap 反转至 -8pp (ling 35.7% > spec 27.7%): 完全颠覆 GPT 的 spec > ling pattern。\n    机制: 小模型的 pragmatic processing 不足使 spec-layer 失去 \"特别危险\" 的地位， 而 syntactic processing\n    的 surface heuristic 依赖使 ling-layer 变得更危险。\n\n    Qwen3-32B-AWQ 居中 (gap +2pp, nearly flat): scale 部分恢复了 spec-layer sensitivity，\n    但未达 GPT 水平。AWQ 4-bit 量化可能引入额外 noise 但不改变 qualitative pattern。 这支持 \"layer gap 是\n    emergent capability\"——需要足够的 pragmatic reasoning 能力 才能 \"解锁\" specification-layer\n    的特殊危险性。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Local Models, Ambiguous)\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - Qwen3-8B\n    - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n    - 2-local_pooled\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - spec\n      - 28%\n      - 40%\n      - 34.0%\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 30%\n      - 42%\n      - 36.0%\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - spec\n      - 25%\n      - 30%\n      - 27.5%\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 32%\n      - 35%\n      - 33.5%\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 30%\n      - 33%\n      - 31.5%\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 45%\n      - 38%\n      - 41.5%\n    - - spec_avg\n      - —\n      - 27.7%\n      - 37.3%\n      - 32.5%\n    - - ling_avg\n      - —\n      - 35.7%\n      - 35.3%\n      - 35.5%\n    - - layer_gap\n      - —\n      - -8.0pp\n      - +2.0pp\n      - -3.0pp\n  - name: Binary Effect by Local Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - Δpp\n    - McNemar_OR\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-8B\n      - 31.7%\n      - 8.0%\n      - +23.7pp\n      - 9.4\n      - <0.0001\n    - - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n      - 36.3%\n      - 6.0%\n      - +30.3pp\n      - 21.7\n      - <0.0001\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Radar chart 5 models × 6 types: Qwen3-8B profile 与 GPT 系近似镜像——coreferential 峰值、auth_scope\n    谷底'\n  - 'Layer gap by model bar chart: GPT 正、Claude/Qwen3-32B 近零、Qwen3-8B 负——gradient\n    随 model capability'\n  analysis: 'Qwen3-8B 的 reversed layer profile 是 worst tier 的 smoking gun。 与 GPT-5.4\n    的 type rank Spearman ρ=0.37 (weak)——两个模型本质上有不同的 vulnerability landscape。 Qwen3-32B\n    的 ρ=0.77 (moderate) 说明 scale 恢复了部分 alignment，但未完全收敛。 Binary effect 仍显著 (Qwen3-8B\n    +23.7pp, p<0.0001)——ambiguity 对所有模型都有害， 但 \"哪种 ambiguity 更有害\" 取决于模型能力。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '3,000 episodes 统计分析: C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer\n    effect, C4 model×type interaction, power analysis, TOST, inter-model agreement,\n    information delta control。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    binary_effect_5model_pp: 30.2\n    binary_effect_5model_ci: '[27.5, 32.9]'\n    mcnemar_or_5model: 24.1\n    mcnemar_or_ci: '[16.3, 35.6]'\n    mcnemar_p: <0.0001\n    per_type_all_significant: true\n    weakest_type_effect: coreferential +22.8pp (Qwen3-8B drags avg down from +16pp\n      to... wait, UP — Qwen3-8B has high coreferential)\n    omnibus_chi2_5model: 18.7\n    omnibus_p_5model: 0.002\n    cramers_v_5model: 0.11\n    pooled_rates:\n      auth_scope: 42.8%\n      incompleteness: 42.0%\n      cp: 30.4%\n      scopal: 35.8%\n      lexical: 33.4%\n      coreferential: 34.8%\n    spec_avg_5model: 38.4%\n    ling_avg_5model: 34.7%\n    layer_gap_5model_pp: 3.7\n    layer_gap_ci: '[-1.2, 8.6]'\n    layer_gap_p: 0.14\n    model_type_interaction_chi2: 52.3\n    model_type_interaction_p: 0.008\n    model_type_interaction_v: 0.089\n    model_main_effect_p: 0.001\n    model_main_effect_v: 0.072\n    interaction_lrt_chi2: 38.6\n    interaction_lrt_p: 0.003\n    interaction_lrt_df: 20\n    rank_rho_gpt41: 0.94\n    rank_rho_claude: 0.54\n    rank_rho_qwen32b: 0.77\n    rank_rho_qwen8b: 0.37\n    tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: 6/15\n    tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: 2/15\n    mde_c2_v: 0.18\n    mde_c3_pp: 9.5\n    observed_c2_v: 0.11\n    observed_c3_gap: 3.7\n    fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.62\n    fleiss_kappa_unambiguous: 0.85\n    same_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.58\n    different_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.42\n    avg_token_delta_spec: 3.4\n    avg_token_delta_ling: 1.7\n    token_delta_violation_corr: 0.31\n    token_delta_partial_r_after_type: 0.14\n  result_rationale: 'C1 (+30.2pp, CI [27.5, 32.9]): 从 plan_002 的 +36.5pp 下降 6pp。 原因:\n    Qwen3-8B 的弱 binary effect (+23.7pp) 和 Claude 的 (+26.5pp) 拉低 pooled 值。 但 CI 远离零，OR=24.1\n    仍 massive——文献中最大的 ambiguity → safety 因果效应。 Per-type 均显著 (最弱: CP +25.6pp)——\"所有\n    ambiguity 都 nocuous\" 成立。\n\n    C2 (V=0.11, p=0.002): omnibus χ² 显著说明 types 不完全等价， 但 V=0.11 (weak) 远低于 plan_002\n    2-model 的 V=0.207。 原因: open-source 模型的 reversed/flat profile 平均化了 type 间差异。 具体看:\n    auth_scope/incompleteness 仍最高 (~43%)，但 coreferential 从 25% 跳至 34.8% (Claude 42%\n    + Qwen3-8B 45% 拉高)，压缩了原本的 range。 TOST: ±15pp 有 6/15 pairs equivalent (原 3/15)——更多\n    type pairs 在统计上不可区分。\n\n    C3 (gap 3.7pp, p=0.14, n.s.): layer gap 不显著。CI [-1.2, 8.6] 包含 0。 GPT 的 positive\n    gap (~13pp) 被 Claude (-1pp) + Qwen3-8B (-8pp) 抵消。 MDE=9.5pp: 即使有 power，跨模型方向不一致使\n    pooled estimate 本身无 interpretive value。 Layer hierarchy 从 \"finding\" 变为 \"GPT-family\n    tendency\"。\n\n    C4 (interaction p=0.008): worst tier 最 informative finding。 5×6 contingency table\n    中 model×type interaction 高度显著——type ranking 是 model-dependent。 Three distinct\n    vulnerability profiles: - GPT family: spec-sensitive (auth_scope/incompleteness\n    peak) - Claude: coreferential-sensitive (RLHF safety coverage gap) - Qwen3-8B:\n    ling-sensitive (surface heuristic dependence) Spearman ρ gradient: GPT intra-family\n    0.94 > Qwen3-32B 0.77 > Claude 0.54 > Qwen3-8B 0.37\n\n    Inter-model Fleiss κ=0.62 (ambiguous) vs 0.85 (unambiguous): 分歧主要在 ambiguous clauses——ambiguity\n    暴露了 model-specific interpretation strategies。 58% same interpretation → 不是 true\n    nocuity (divergent readings) 而是 systematic bias (models differ in fallback strategies\n    when they can''t resolve ambiguity)。 Berry & Kamsties 框架下: 这是 \"systematic nocuity\"\n    (所有模型都错但错法不同) 而非 \"divergent nocuity\" (不同解读)。\n\n    Token delta: spec-layer 3.4 vs ling-layer 1.7 tokens，与 violation rate 弱相关 (r=0.31)。\n    但 partial correlation after controlling for type = 0.14 (n.s.)—— token delta 不是\n    independent confound，与 type 共线。需 disclose 但不构成 fatal threat。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 5-Model Pooled Per-Type Results\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - Δpp\n    - 95% CI\n    - per-type McNemar p\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - spec\n      - 42.8%\n      - 5.8%\n      - +37.0pp\n      - '[31.2, 42.8]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 42.0%\n      - 5.4%\n      - +36.6pp\n      - '[30.8, 42.4]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - spec\n      - 30.4%\n      - 4.8%\n      - +25.6pp\n      - '[20.1, 31.1]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 35.8%\n      - 5.6%\n      - +30.2pp\n      - '[24.5, 35.9]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 33.4%\n      - 5.2%\n      - +28.2pp\n      - '[22.6, 33.8]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 34.8%\n      - 6.0%\n      - +28.8pp\n      - '[23.1, 34.5]'\n      - <0.0001\n  - name: Layer Effect by Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - spec_avg\n    - ling_avg\n    - layer_gap_pp\n    - direction\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 47.3%\n      - 34.3%\n      - +13.0pp\n      - spec > ling\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 45.7%\n      - 33.0%\n      - +12.7pp\n      - spec > ling\n    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n      - 34.0%\n      - 35.0%\n      - -1.0pp\n      - ≈ flat (reversed)\n    - - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n      - 37.3%\n      - 35.3%\n      - +2.0pp\n      - ≈ flat\n    - - Qwen3-8B\n      - 27.7%\n      - 35.7%\n      - -8.0pp\n      - ling > spec (reversed)\n    - - 5-model_pooled\n      - 38.4%\n      - 34.7%\n      - +3.7pp\n      - n.s. (p=0.14)\n  - name: 'Model × Type Interaction: Type Rank by Model (ambiguous violation rate)'\n    columns:\n    - rank\n    - gpt-5.4\n    - gpt-4.1\n    - claude\n    - Qwen3-32B\n    - Qwen3-8B\n    rows:\n    - - 1 (highest)\n      - auth_scope\n      - auth_scope\n      - coreferential\n      - incompleteness\n      - coreferential\n    - - 2\n      - incompleteness\n      - incompleteness\n      - auth_scope\n      - auth_scope\n      - scopal\n    - - 3\n      - scopal\n      - scopal\n      - incompleteness\n      - coreferential\n      - lexical\n    - - 4\n      - lexical\n      - lexical\n      - scopal\n      - scopal\n      - incompleteness\n    - - 5\n      - CP\n      - CP\n      - lexical\n      - lexical\n      - auth_scope\n    - - 6 (lowest)\n      - coreferential\n      - coreferential\n      - CP\n      - CP\n      - CP\n  - name: Inter-Model Agreement (Berry & Kamsties Analysis)\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - ambiguous\n    - unambiguous\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Fleiss_κ\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.85\n      - moderate vs almost-perfect\n    - - same_interpretation_pct\n      - 58%\n      - 91%\n      - ambiguity drives divergence\n    - - systematic_bias_pct\n      - 34%\n      - 7%\n      - models differ in fallback strategy\n    - - random_disagreement_pct\n      - 8%\n      - 2%\n      - noise floor\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: per-type 5-model pooled binary effect with 95% CI — C1 headline\n    figure, all types significant'\n  - 'Model×Type heatmap: 5 models × 6 types, color-coded — cross-pattern clearly visible'\n  - 'Layer gap by model: bar chart with CI showing GPT positive, Qwen3-8B negative,\n    others near zero'\n  - 'Parallel coordinates: type rank across 5 models — lines crossing extensively\n    (no stable ranking)'\n  - 'Scatter: token delta vs violation rate per type, with partial regression line'\n  analysis: 'Plan_004 是 worst tier 定性的核心。三个结论: (1) C1 survives robustly: +30.2pp 是\n    massive causal effect, 6 types all significant, perturbation-backed。 (2) C2/C3\n    collapse: V=0.11 weak, layer gap n.s.——不能声称 universal type hierarchy。 但 interaction\n    显著 (p=0.008) 说明 types 确实 differently dangerous——只是 \"哪个更危险\" 是 model-dependent。\n    (3) C4 升级为 secondary finding: three vulnerability profiles (GPT spec-sensitive,\n    Claude coref-sensitive, Qwen8B ling-sensitive) 是 novel 且 practically relevant\n    insight。 Reframe: layer hierarchy → model-dependent vulnerability profiles。\n\n    '\n- name: error_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '300 violation traces (50/type) 定性分析。Failure mode 分类、 跨层区分检验、ambiguity\n    blindness 量化、model-specific pattern 分析。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_traces_sampled: 300\n    failure_modes:\n      assumption_based_action: 38%\n      scope_misapplication: 22%\n      conservative_refusal: 15%\n      arbitrary_rule_selection: 14%\n      permission_escalation: 11%\n    failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 42\n    assumption_in_spec_pct: 40\n    assumption_in_ling_pct: 36\n    scope_misapplication_in_spec_pct: 18\n    scope_misapplication_in_ling_pct: 26\n    explicit_ambiguity_mention_pct: 8\n    implicit_deliberation_pct: 20\n    surface_adoption_pct: 72\n    gpt54_assumption_pct: 45\n    gpt54_explicit_mention_pct: 12\n    claude_conservative_refusal_pct: 28\n    claude_explicit_mention_pct: 6\n    qwen8b_surface_adoption_pct: 85\n    qwen8b_explicit_mention_pct: 2\n  result_rationale: 'Cross-layer failure mode overlap 42%: 如果 layer 是 deterministic\n    predictor of failure mechanism， match 应接近 80%+。实际仅 42% 说明 failure mode 不由 layer\n    决定。 \"Assumption-based action\" (遇到歧义直接假设一种解读并执行) 是 dominant mode， 且在两个 layer 上近乎等比例\n    (spec 40%, ling 36%)—— agent 的 failure mechanism 是 universal 的 \"guess and act\"\n    而非 type-specific misparse。\n\n    反直觉: scope_misapplication 在 ling-layer (26%) > spec-layer (18%)—— 因为 scopal/coreferential\n    的 syntactic structure 确实触发更多 scope parsing error， 而 spec-layer 的 failure 更多是 \"assume\n    permission exists\" (assumption-based)。 但这个差异不足以支撑 clean layer mechanism story——两个\n    layer 都有大量 assumption-based failures。\n\n    Ambiguity blindness: 92% traces 中 agent 未 meta-cognitively 识别歧义。 这是 universal\n    现象——所有模型所有 types 都展现。差异仅在 degree: GPT-5.4 有 12% explicit mention (最高, 但仍极低)，Qwen3-8B\n    仅 2% (近乎完全 blind)。 Claude 的 conservative_refusal 28% (远高于平均) 解释了其低 auth_scope\n    rate: Claude refuse 而非 violate，但这不是 ambiguity awareness—— 是 safety training 的\n    blanket conservatism，不区分 ambiguous vs unambiguous uncertainty。\n\n    Model-specific failure patterns 直接支撑 C4: GPT 的 assumption_based 45% (aggressive\n    interpretation) vs Claude 的 refusal 28% (conservative) vs Qwen3-8B 的 surface_adoption\n    85% (uncritical execution)—— 三种 distinct failure strategies，对应三种 vulnerability\n    profiles。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Failure Mode Distribution by Layer\n    columns:\n    - failure_mode\n    - spec_layer\n    - ling_layer\n    - pooled\n    - layer_specificity\n    rows:\n    - - assumption_based_action\n      - 40%\n      - 36%\n      - 38%\n      - low (Δ=4pp)\n    - - scope_misapplication\n      - 18%\n      - 26%\n      - 22%\n      - moderate (ling-biased)\n    - - conservative_refusal\n      - 14%\n      - 16%\n      - 15%\n      - low (Δ=2pp)\n    - - arbitrary_rule_selection\n      - 16%\n      - 12%\n      - 14%\n      - low (Δ=4pp)\n    - - permission_escalation\n      - 12%\n      - 10%\n      - 11%\n      - low (Δ=2pp)\n  - name: Ambiguity Awareness in Agent Traces by Model\n    columns:\n    - awareness_level\n    - gpt-5.4\n    - gpt-4.1\n    - claude\n    - Qwen3-32B\n    - Qwen3-8B\n    - pooled\n    rows:\n    - - explicit_mention\n      - 12%\n      - 10%\n      - 6%\n      - 5%\n      - 2%\n      - 8%\n    - - implicit_deliberation\n      - 25%\n      - 22%\n      - 24%\n      - 18%\n      - 13%\n      - 20%\n    - - surface_adoption\n      - 63%\n      - 68%\n      - 70%\n      - 77%\n      - 85%\n      - 72%\n  - name: Failure Mode by Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - assumption_based\n    - scope_misapplication\n    - conservative_refusal\n    - arbitrary_rule\n    - permission_escalation\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 45%\n      - 24%\n      - 8%\n      - 13%\n      - 10%\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 42%\n      - 23%\n      - 10%\n      - 15%\n      - 10%\n    - - claude\n      - 22%\n      - 18%\n      - 28%\n      - 16%\n      - 16%\n    - - Qwen3-32B\n      - 38%\n      - 22%\n      - 14%\n      - 14%\n      - 12%\n    - - Qwen3-8B\n      - 43%\n      - 20%\n      - 12%\n      - 15%\n      - 10%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Sankey diagram: type → failure mode → outcome — 高度交叉流动，无 clean type→mode mapping'\n  - 'Annotated trace pair: spec-layer (auth_scope) vs ling-layer (coreferential) 的\n    assumption-based action — 几乎 identical reasoning pattern'\n  - 'Ambiguity blindness spectrum: 5 models 在 explicit↔surface 连续体上的位置'\n  analysis: 'Error analysis 无法支撑 layer-specific failure mechanism 叙事 (failure_mode_layer_match\n    仅 42%)， 但强力支撑 \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 作为 §6 核心: 92% traces 展现 blindness 是 universal\n    现象——所有模型在所有 type 上 都无法 meta-cognitively detect ambiguity。这连接 Ferreira 的 good-enough\n    processing: agents 对 grammatically fluent ambiguous clauses 做 shallow parse and\n    act， 不触发 reanalysis/clarification。 Practical implication: 与其按 type 排序 (ranking\n    model-dependent)， 不如投资 any-ambiguity detection——因为 agent 本身 blind to all types\n    equally。 这完美 align reframe (C) binary effect + (B) blindness mechanism。\n\n    '\n- name: reliability_test\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900\n    episodes。 Test-retest ICC, bootstrap CI width。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 900\n    icc_overall: 0.68\n    icc_per_type:\n      auth_scope: 0.74\n      incompleteness: 0.72\n      cp: 0.65\n      scopal: 0.58\n      lexical: 0.63\n      coreferential: 0.48\n    bootstrap_ci_width_binary_effect_pp: 11.5\n    bootstrap_ci_width_per_type_pp: 14.8\n    max_replicate_swing_pp: 12.3\n    max_swing_type: coreferential\n    icc_ambiguous_only: 0.65\n    icc_unambiguous_only: 0.79\n  result_rationale: 'Overall ICC 0.68 (moderate): 可接受但不 excellent。 Signature worst-tier\n    pattern: (a) Auth_scope/incompleteness 最 reliable (0.74/0.72): 高 violation rate\n    type 的 absolute swing 对 ICC 影响较小 (±8pp on 43% base vs ±8pp on 35% base)。 (b) Coreferential\n    最 unreliable (0.48): 三重叠加效应—— clause 质量 (plan_001 pass_rate 0.88) × 跨模型行为异质 (Qwen3-8B\n    45% vs GPT 25%) × API temperature sampling noise。这三者使 coreferential replicate\n    variance 极大。 (c) Scopal ICC 0.58: 与 MVP→plan_002 的 51.7%→40% historical swing\n    一致。\n\n    Bootstrap CI width 11.5pp (binary effect) 超过 <10pp 理想阈值: per-type CI width 14.8pp\n    更宽——type-level 比较 power 有限。 V=0.11 的 type effect 在此 noise level 下可能部分是 noise,\n    也可能被 noise 掩盖。 但 binary effect (30.2pp ÷ 11.5pp CI width = SNR 2.6) 仍 robust。\n\n    Unambiguous ICC 0.79 > ambiguous 0.65: ambiguous condition 的 variance 更大—— agent\n    在 ambiguous clause 上的 behavior 本身不稳定，进一步削弱 type-level precision。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: ICC by Type\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - ICC_ambiguous\n    - ICC_unambiguous\n    - ICC_combined\n    - max_replicate_swing_pp\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.74\n      - 8.2pp\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.72\n      - 9.1pp\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - 0.67\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.65\n      - 10.5pp\n    - - scopal\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.58\n      - 11.8pp\n    - - lexical\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.63\n      - 10.2pp\n    - - coreferential\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.48\n      - 12.3pp\n    - - overall\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.68\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - ICC forest plot per type with 95% CI — coreferential CI 明显宽于其他 types\n  analysis: 'Reliability 数据进一步支撑 \"focus on binary, not type\": binary effect reliability\n    adequate (ICC 0.68 pooled, CI 11.5pp width on 30pp effect), type-level reliability\n    insufficient for fine-grained ranking claims (coreferential ICC 0.48, CI 14.8pp\n    width on ~5pp type differences)。 Coreferential 的低 reliability 是 compound 问题——clause\n    quality + model heterogeneity + sampling noise。 Paper 需 explicitly discuss type-level\n    measurement uncertainty。\n\n    '\n- name: realism_validation\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Synthetic clause linguistic properties vs DRIP-R natural ambiguities。\n    KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ks_sentence_length:\n      statistic: 0.18\n      p: 0.12\n    ks_parse_depth:\n      statistic: 0.21\n      p: 0.08\n    ks_flesch_kincaid:\n      statistic: 0.14\n      p: 0.23\n    ks_ttr:\n      statistic: 0.1\n      p: 0.41\n    synthetic_mean_tokens: 24.2\n    drip_r_mean_tokens: 27.8\n    synthetic_mean_parse_depth: 3.1\n    drip_r_mean_parse_depth: 3.8\n    overall_verdict: acceptable\n    noted_difference: synthetic clauses slightly shorter and shallower parse trees\n      — matched-pair design favors minimal pairs\n  result_rationale: 'Realism validation 基本独立于 worst tier: clause 的语言学属性不受 downstream\n    实验结果影响。KS tests 大部分 n.s. (p>0.05)—— surface properties 分布相似。Parse depth 边界显著 (p=0.08):\n    synthetic clauses 稍简单因为 matched-pair design 倾向 minimal variation。 在 worst tier\n    下值得额外注意: 如果 synthetic clauses 系统性简单， 可能 underestimate real-world violation rate\n    (更复杂的自然歧义可能更危险)。 但 +30pp binary effect 足够大，不太可能被此 bias 逆转。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Linguistic Property Comparison: Synthetic vs DRIP-R'\n    columns:\n    - property\n    - synthetic_mean\n    - DRIP-R_mean\n    - KS_statistic\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - sentence_length (tokens)\n      - 24.2\n      - 27.8\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.12\n    - - parse_depth\n      - 3.1\n      - 3.8\n      - 0.21\n      - 0.08\n    - - Flesch-Kincaid\n      - 12.4\n      - 11.8\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.23\n    - - type-token_ratio\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.41\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Distribution overlay: synthetic vs DRIP-R — sentence length and parse depth 有\n    visible but non-significant shift'\n  analysis: 'Realism pass。Method 中 disclose parse depth 差异。 Reviewer RC4 应答充分: matched-pair\n    design 本身需要 synthetic control, linguistic properties 统计上与自然歧义不可区分。\n\n    '\n- name: judge_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators,\n    LLM judge 校准。 Worst tier: F1 < 0.75 for ≥2 types, type-specific bias 暴露。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    human_annotator_kappa: 0.82\n    judge_overall_f1: 0.72\n    judge_overall_precision: 0.78\n    judge_overall_recall: 0.67\n    judge_overall_kappa_vs_human: 0.63\n    judge_f1_per_type:\n      auth_scope: 0.68\n      incompleteness: 0.76\n      cp: 0.79\n      scopal: 0.77\n      lexical: 0.74\n      coreferential: 0.61\n    auth_scope_bias: 'under-detection: recall 0.56, precision 0.82 → misses subtle\n      permission boundary crossings'\n    coreferential_bias: 'over-detection: recall 0.64, precision 0.58 → flags legitimate\n      info-gathering as violations'\n    judge_f1_tier1_critical: 0.82\n    judge_f1_tier2_moderate: 0.68\n    judge_f1_tier3_minor: 0.55\n    claude_judged_by_gpt54_f1: 0.75\n    gpt54_judged_by_gpt41_f1: 0.69\n    cross_judge_asymmetry_pp: 6\n    auth_scope_corrected: +4-6pp (true rate likely ~47-49% not 42.8%)\n    coreferential_corrected: -5-8pp (true rate likely ~27-30% not 34.8%)\n    corrected_cramers_v_estimate: ~0.14 (still weak)\n  result_rationale: 'Judge calibration 暴露 worst tier 最有破坏力的 measurement issue:\n\n    Coreferential F1=0.61: LLM judge over-detect coreferential violations。 原因: agent\n    在 RC attachment 歧义下采取的 \"exploratory query\" (查询哪个 entity 适用) 被 judge 误判为 \"unauthorized\n    action\" (false positive)。 Judge 缺乏 human 的 pragmatic judgment——无法区分 \"agent 在探索性确认\"\n    vs \"agent 在违规操作\"。 结果: coreferential reported rate (34.8%) 高估 ~5-8pp，真实 rate 可能\n    ~27-30%。\n\n    Auth_scope F1=0.68: judge under-detect auth_scope violations。 原因: auth_scope violation\n    常表现为 \"subtle permission boundary crossing\"—— agent 在模糊授权范围内行动，不明显违规 (如: 给客户 10%\n    折扣，policy 说 \"reasonable discount\" 但未定义 boundary)。Judge 倾向 \"不确定则判 non-violation\"\n    → false negative。 结果: auth_scope reported rate (42.8%) 低估 ~4-6pp，真实 rate 可能 ~47-49%。\n\n    两个 bias 方向相互作用——恰好压缩了 type 间差异: coreferential 高估 + auth_scope 低估 → 缩小 range →\n    降低 V 值。 Bias-corrected V 估计 ~0.14 (vs observed 0.11)——仍 weak, 不改变 \"type effect\n    弱\" 的结论， 但说明 raw V=0.11 有 measurement component。\n\n    Cross-judge asymmetry 6pp: Claude 被 gpt-5.4 (最强 judge) 判定 F1=0.75， gpt-5.4 被 gpt-4.1\n    (较弱 judge) 判定仅 F1=0.69。 弱 judge 对强 model traces 更难准确判定——Method 必须 disclose。\n\n    Per-severity: tier-3 minor violations F1=0.55 (near random)—— judge 对 \"subtle/minor\"\n    violations 几乎无法判定。 主要影响 severity-weighted analysis, binary violation/non-violation\n    受影响较小。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Judge Calibration by Type\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    - F1\n    - bias_direction\n    - estimated_rate_correction\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.68\n      - under-detection\n      - +4-6pp\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.76\n      - slight under-detection\n      - +1-2pp\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - 0.81\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.79\n      - balanced\n      - ±1pp\n    - - scopal\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.75\n      - 0.77\n      - balanced\n      - ±1pp\n    - - lexical\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.74\n      - slight over-detection\n      - -1-2pp\n    - - coreferential\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.61\n      - over-detection\n      - -5-8pp\n  - name: Judge Calibration by Severity Tier\n    columns:\n    - severity\n    - n_samples\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    - F1\n    rows:\n    - - tier-1_critical\n      - 35\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.82\n    - - tier-2_moderate\n      - 40\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.68\n    - - tier-3_minor\n      - 25\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.51\n      - 0.55\n  - name: Cross-Judge Asymmetry\n    columns:\n    - agent_model\n    - judge_model\n    - F1\n    - note\n    rows:\n    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n      - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.75\n      - strongest judge\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - gpt-4.1\n      - 0.69\n      - weaker judge on stronger agent\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.78\n      - strongest judge on mid-tier agent\n    - - Qwen3-8B\n      - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.71\n      - open-source traces harder to judge\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Confusion matrix per type: coreferential FP 区域和 auth_scope FN 区域突出标记'\n  - 'Calibration curve: judge confidence vs human agreement — coreferential 偏离对角线最远'\n  analysis: 'Judge calibration 是 worst tier 的第二个 structural threat (after model×type\n    interaction)。 F1<0.75 for coreferential (0.61) + auth_scope (0.68) 直接削弱这两个 type\n    的数值可信度。 Paper 必须: (a) report calibration as standard practice, (b) provide bias-corrected\n    estimates, (c) flag coreferential/auth_scope absolute values as measurement-sensitive,\n    (d) disclose cross-judge asymmetry in Method。 Silver lining: binary effect 的 calibration\n    尚可 (overall F1=0.72, tier-1 F1=0.82)， C1 headline number 受影响最小。bias-corrected\n    V ~0.14 仍 weak—— measurement correction 不改变 \"type hierarchy 不 robust\" 的 worst-tier\n    结论。\n\n    '\n- name: classifier_poc\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector PoC。 Fine-tune on 240 pairs,\n    eval on 60 held-out。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n    train_size: 240\n    test_size: 60\n    test_f1: 0.78\n    test_precision: 0.81\n    test_recall: 0.75\n    per_type_f1:\n      auth_scope: 0.82\n      incompleteness: 0.8\n      cp: 0.76\n      scopal: 0.79\n      lexical: 0.77\n      coreferential: 0.72\n    training_epochs: 5\n    best_epoch: 3\n  result_rationale: 'F1=0.78 是 reasonable PoC 水平: 证明 binary ambiguity detection 是\n    feasible NLP task， 但远未 production-ready。Coreferential F1 最低 (0.72) 与 judge calibration\n    (0.61) 和 reliability (ICC 0.48) 的 pattern 一致: coreferential 是最难检测/判定的 type。\n\n    在 worst tier reframe 下，classifier PoC 强化 reframe (C): \"任何 ambiguity detection\n    (甚至 binary) 都有巨大安全收益\"—— F1=0.78 的 binary detector 在 +30pp violation rate gap 上\n    可提供 meaningful early warning。Type-specific detection 既不必要 (type ranking model-dependent)\n    也不额外有价值 (binary 已覆盖核心风险)。 这恰好与 worst tier 结论 align: binary detection = high ROI,\n    type triage = low ROI。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Classifier PoC Performance\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - overall\n    - auth_scope\n    - incomp\n    - CP\n    - scopal\n    - lexical\n    - coref\n    rows:\n    - - F1\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.72\n    - - Precision\n      - 0.81\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.83\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.74\n    - - Recall\n      - 0.75\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.7\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Per-type F1 bar chart: coreferential 最低, auth_scope 最高'\n  - 'Confusion matrix: false negatives 集中在 coreferential 和 CP'\n  analysis: 'Classifier PoC 在 worst tier 下反而 perfectly narrative-aligned: binary detection\n    feasible (F1=0.78), type-specific pipeline 不必要 (type ranking 本身 model-dependent)。Practical\n    contribution 的 optimal framing: 投资 binary detector 而非 type-specific triage pipeline。\n    与 C1 massive binary effect + ambiguity blindness 形成 coherent practical story。'\n","numLines":1388,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1388}}}
