{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AZLD9sDZARkUv1KFhHCoRQ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/report.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Handover — 2026-05-20\\\\n\\\\n> 由 Agent 生成，每次状态变更后自动更新。硬限 150 行。\\\\n\\\\n## 运行中\\\\n（无）\\\\n\\\\n## 待处理\\\\n- plan_009: Cross-judge LLM agreement (gpt-5.4 vs gpt-4.1) achieves substantial agreement (weighted κ ≥ 0.60) on violation level classification. LLM-human agreement should be comparable, validating the cross-judge evaluation design.（准备中）\\\\n\\\\n## 近期结论\\\\n- **plan_006** (success): API model violation judgments are highly reproducible across independent replicates (ICC ≥ 0.75), confirming that the observed violation rates and type differences in plan_002 are stable signals, not sampling noise. ← 基于 plan_002\\\\n  [plan_006_icc_results](/api/workspace-files/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/plan_006/report/icc_results.json)\\\\n- **plan_005** (success): Specification-layer ambiguities produce qualitatively different failure modes (more assumption_based_action) than linguistic-layer ambiguities (more scope_misapplication), and coreferential's low violation rate is explained by higher conservative_refusal rate. These distinct failure mode profiles explain the layer hierarchy (spec ~46pp vs ling ~27pp). ← 基于 plan_002\\\\n  [plan_005_failure_modes](/api/workspace-files/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/plan_005/data/failure_modes.jsonl) | [plan_005_summary](/api/workspace-files/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/plan_005/report/summary.json)\\\\n- **plan_002** (negative): Policy ambiguity causes significantly higher agent safety violation rates (+30-40pp) across all 6 ambiguity types, with uniform effect size across types (no significant type×violation interaction). Binary effect is the primary finding; type uniformity supports that ambiguity per se, not specific linguistic structures, drives violations.\\\\n  [plan_002 full study results](/api/workspace-files/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/plan_002/data/full_statistics.json) | [c3_layer_effect_test](/api/workspace-files/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/plan_002/report/layer_effect_test.json)\\\\n\\\\n## 趋势\\\\n成功 2 / 负向 3 / 失败 0 / 共 5\\\\n\\\\n## 下一步\\\\n（无活跃 idea，请通过 ideas.md 添加）\\\\n\\\\n## 资源状态\\\\n（无服务器配置）\\\\n\\\\n## 告警\\\\n（无）\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2064, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NAfSUwSFFqdiz2bg84riqy","session_id":"bd96f57a-80ec-4566-95cb-ccf252e77f7a","uuid":"79b5b666-9a5b-4bda-9bda-6137c2ebe78f","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:51:35.866Z"}
